A||||71||Homicidal||Fiero Lovers SURVEY!  You ALL better take it!||||10||
Z||000000||Homicidal||05-09-2000||07:01 PM||||1. When did you start to like Fieros?<P>2. Why did you like them?<P>3. When and where did you first obtain your first Fiero?<P>4. What type of Fiero do you own?<P>5. What year and model do you like the best?<P>6. Do you have a nice paint job on it?<P>7. What does it run like?<P>8. Do you get "looks" when driving your Fiero?<P>9. What sound system do you have in your Fiero?<P>10. Do your relatives and friends like Fieros?<P>11.  Your Fiero?<P>12. Why do you think they cancelled the car (short answer please)?<P>13. Do you want a new Fiero to be released?<P>14. If so, what would you want it to look like?<P>15. What plans do you have for your Fiero, in terms of upgrades, engine work, body kits, sound system, etc..<P>16. Do you think Fiero's will rise in collectors value?<P>17. If and when your Fiero finally does break down for good, will you keep it or junk it?||||reg||10
Z||000001||Homicidal||05-09-2000||07:10 PM||||1. When did you start to like Fieros? <B> Just last year!<P>2. Why did you like them?[b] At first it was just "a car."  But the sheer fun in driving my speedy demon, I just fell in love with it!</B><P>3. When and where did you first obtain your first Fiero?<B> Albertsons Supermarket parking lot, June 1999.</B><P>4. What type of Fiero do you own?<B> 1984 SE, Glossy White paint job, brown interior, perfect condition!</B><P>5. What year and model do you like the best?<B> I like any year with the Coupe/SE design, I never got into the later year GT's since I really don't like the rounded back.</B><P>6. Do you have a nice paint job on it? <B> Oh HELL yah!  $800 job!</B><P>7. What does it run like?<B> Besides for the recent clutch problem and a loose starter cable, it has been running GREAT!  Idles at 1000 and has great pickup and stopping!</B><P>8. Do you get "looks" when driving your Fiero?<B> Yes and no.  Most looks come from the bass.</B><P>9. What sound system do you have in your Fiero? <B> JVC 12 CD Changer + Headunit and a 10" Polk Audio db Series subwoofer behind the seat.  Can we say..."thump"?</B><P>10. Do your relatives and friends like Fieros?<B> My dad does and so does my best friend Daniel.  Besides that, not really.</B><P>11.  Your Fiero? <B>My dad loves it, my mom is okay with it, my sister think it's "too small."  My gf likes it, but doesn't like the size.</B><P>12. Why do you think they cancelled the car (short answer please)? <B> High insurance rates.</B><P>13. Do you want a new Fiero to be released?<B> Yes and no.  I would like to see a new design ever since I saw the Prototype "89" Fiero.  But no because some cars should remain classics!</B><P>14. If so, what would you want it to look like? <B> More streamlined, similiar to Trans-Am.  And a TAD bit bigger.  Possibly engine in the front.  Interior should remain almost the same.</B><P>15. What plans do you have for your Fiero, in terms of upgrades, engine work, body kits, sound system, etc..<B> None anymore.  Just good matienence.  I do plan to install two new 4X10's though.  New seat covers, and fix my headlight motors.  Also get a new rear tailight cover.</B><P>16. Do you think Fiero's will rise in collectors value?<B> Yes, people are starting to see how well made they can be and their exotic look and ability to be easily modified peaks people's interest I think.</B><P>17. If and when your Fiero finally does break down for good, will you keep it or junk it?<B> Keep it, no doubt.  I have no real reason to junk it and it could be a cool side project to drop a v-8 into it.  I would kick myself if I junked it and they rose in value!</B><p>[This message has been edited by Homicidal (edited 05-09-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000002||DaRkLoRD||05-09-2000||07:39 PM||||1. When did you start to like Fieros?<BR><B>1991.. I saw one in Detroit and wanted to get one.</B><P>2. Why did you like them?<BR><B>unique styling, fair bit of power.. and awesome handling!</B><P>3. When and where did you first obtain your first Fiero?<BR><B>don't have one yet...  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"></B><P>4. What type of Fiero do you own?<BR><B>see above...</B><P>5. What year and model do you like the best?<BR><B>87 GT.. 88s look the best IMHO, but there are more aftermarket parts for the pre-88s..<P>of course if I found a nice 88 GT for a good price, I wouldn't turn it down!!<BR></B><P>6. Do you have a nice paint job on it?<BR><B>you don't listen, do you? hehe..</B><P>7. What does it run like?<BR><B>I drove Dave's 86 GT, it ran pretty good.. except for the brakes.. heh.</B><P>8. Do you get "looks" when driving your Fiero?<BR><B>some people waved at me when I was in one on sunday.. said "hey look, there's 4 of them!" (we were driving around the town)</B><P>9. What sound system do you have in your Fiero?<BR><B>I want a monster sound system.. I wanna rattle windows.. hehe..</B><P>10. Do your relatives and friends like Fieros?<BR><B>my dad doesn't like them.. he likes fords. ugh.</B><P>11. Your Fiero?<BR><B>don't have one yet, but I'm getting a black GT in a few months!</B><P>12. Why do you think they cancelled the car (short answer please)?<BR><B>I've heard lots of reasons..</B><P>13. Do you want a new Fiero to be released?<BR><B>I doubt one would be.</B><P>14. If so, what would you want it to look like?<BR><B>sorta like a 2nd gen MR2, only better.. hehe</B><P>15. What plans do you have for your Fiero, in terms of upgrades, engine work, body kits, sound system, etc..<BR><B>Tom's decklid scoop.. 17" alloy 5-spoke wheels.. IRM sidescoops.. low profile popup headlights.. custom interior..</B><P>16. Do you think Fiero's will rise in collectors value?<BR><B>not mine, I'm gonna modify the cr@p out of it.. LOL</B><P>17. If and when your Fiero finally does break down for good, will you keep it or junk it?<BR><B>not sure. depends if I can buy another one.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"></B>||||reg||10
Z||000003||RiceCooker||05-09-2000||07:39 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Homicidal:<BR><B>1. When did you start to like Fieros? When i got one last year<P>2. Why did you like them? looks, handling, power <P>3. When and where did you first obtain your first Fiero? April 1999 from my Aunt/Godmother for next to nothing<P>4. What type of Fiero do you own? Silver 86se  4spd. 16x7.5 TSW blades with 225/40 Pirelli P7000's alpine alarm with dual stage proximity & impact sensor<P>5. What year and model do you like the best? 86-88 GT<P>6. Do you have a nice paint job on it? Factory paint still looks great<P>7. What does it run like? ask the riceboys<P>8. Do you get "looks" when driving your Fiero? Ohhhhhh, yeaaaaaa<P>9. What sound system do you have in your Fiero? JVC head unit with 12 disc changer (mounted in passenger footwell) JBL 4x10 & 4x6<P>10. Do your relatives and friends like Fieros? Ya. They get sick of me always talkin about them.<P>11.  Your Fiero? Most of em are jealous<P>12. Why do you think they cancelled the car (short answer please)? Bad reputation <P>13. Do you want a new Fiero to be released? Nope. they couldn't beat the original. they would just wreck the legacy (300M!!! barf)<P>14. If so, what would you want it to look like?<P>15. What plans do you have for your Fiero, in terms of upgrades, engine work, body kits, sound system, etc.. Headers and entire exhaust system custom made.(next week) Hypertech perf. chip, lower 1" - 1.5", convert to fastback, paint thunderbolt blue <P>16. Do you think Fiero's will rise in collectors value? Over time, yes<P>17. If and when your Fiero finally does break down for good, will you keep it or junk it? Three words: "Hello Mr. Archie"</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>||||reg||6
Z||000004||Sillhouette.com||05-09-2000||07:44 PM||||1. When did you start to like Fieros?<BR>1993<P>2. Why did you like them?<BR>They look like no other car out there.<P>3. When and where did you first obtain your first Fiero?<BR>1999 January from a guy that really needed the money.<P>4. What type of Fiero do you own?<BR>1987 GT<P>5. What year and model do you like the best?<BR>1987 GT<P>6. Do you have a nice paint job on it?<BR>1995 Viper GTS blue<P>7. What does it run like?<BR>Bored out 3.3 with shaved heads shorty headers roller rockers larger throttle body cold air intake with K&N filter on it MSD ignition module Rapid fire spark plugs stainless steel exhaust with larger cat and resonated tips centerforce clutch with monzie 5 speed suspension techniques lowering springs KYB struts polished calipers braided brake lines carbon metallic pads slotted rotors front and rear sway bars with urethan bushings everywhere.  <P>You tell me how it runs.....<P>8. Do you get "looks" when driving your Fiero?<BR>Yes<P>9. What sound system do you have in your Fiero?<BR>Clarion competion with an ORION 10" sub in the kick panel by the passengers foot.<P>10. Do your relatives and friends like Fieros?<BR>No<P>11.  Your Fiero?<BR>Yes<P>12. Why do you think they cancelled the car (short answer please)?<BR>Sold the pattent to the mid engine design to Toyota<P>13. Do you want a new Fiero to be released?<BR>No<P>14. If so, what would you want it to look like?<BR>See answer above<P>15. What plans do you have for your Fiero, in terms of upgrades, engine work, body kits, sound system, etc..<BR>No body kits.  I think that the car look much better the way it is without trying to make it look like what it is not  (ferrari lamborgini and so on)<BR>Much better modding the 2.8 than trying to add all sort of V8 and supercharger V6 setups<BR>Pretty much done with it I'll just beat the living daylights out of it..<P><BR>16. Do you think Fiero's will rise in collectors value?<BR>Yes already had an offer for 18,000 bought it for 3,000 sunk into it 8,000<P>17. If and when your Fiero finally does break down for good, will you keep it or junk it?<BR>My fiero will never break down for good too simple of a car not to be able to fix it. Unless it has some sort of a body kit on it that chopped up all the required strong parts.<P> <P>||||reg||1
Z||000005||Richard Parnell||05-09-2000||08:15 PM||||1. When did you start to like Fieros?<BR>5-6 years ago.  I liked the way they looked but every time I checked one out up close they were crap.  Until I found my baby, it was 1996, a beautiful day in Kaneohe and I went to check out an 87 coupe for sale.  The owner was a moron.  I asked what he wanted , he said "I'd like 1500 but I'll take 1000" Duh, guess what he got.<P>2. Why did you like them?<BR>Liked the way they looked especially my sc with the gold paint job. They handle like a go cart. Plus my golf clubs fit in the storage space behind the engine.<P>3. When and where did you first obtain your first Fiero?<BR>See above.<P>4. What type of Fiero do you own?<BR>87 SC Gold,4 cyl. 5 speed<P>5. What year and model do you like the best?<BR>87 SC Gold, 4 cyl. 5 speed<P>6. Do you have a nice paint job on it?<BR>Fair, the roof and trunk are oxidizing under the clearcoat.<P>7. What does it run like?<BR>Runs strong for a 4 banger.<P>8. Do you get "looks" when driving your Fiero?<BR>Oh yeah.  Mostly from ricers. I think cause it sits so low with nice wide tires on 15" honeycomb rims.<P>9. What sound system do you have in your Fiero?<BR>Mostly stock, new front speakers and an Alpine CD/radio. Sounds good.  I really don'y play the CD much, I'd rather drive with the windows down listening to the engine. Haven't listened to the radio since they discontinued Mark and Brian here in Hawaii.<P>10. Do your relatives and friends like Fieros?<BR>My wife hates the car, every time I have a battle with the clutch system she gets all smug. My sons and nephew think it's cool.<P>11. Your Fiero?<BR>My Fiero what?<P>12. Why do you think they cancelled the car (short answer please)?<BR>No foresight on the part of GM. Fine with me.  It's not like with Camaros where there are a million of them running around.<P>13. Do you want a new Fiero to be released?<BR>No<P>14. If so, what would you want it to look like?<BR>87 SC Gold, 4 cyl.(maybe V8) 5 speed<P>15. What plans do you have for your Fiero, in terms of upgrades, engine work, body kits, sound system, etc..<BR>350 V8. Some body panel replacement, new paint, suspension upgrade, electric windows, electric door locks. Would like to put in that cool looking headlight setup that Tom  (I think) sells.<P>16. Do you think Fiero's will rise in collectors value?<BR>They already are.  Up to a year ago Fieros were for sale in the paper every day and cheap.  Now I haven't seen one the the paper this year. One mechanic in town who has a V8 in one, has 4-5 Fieros.<P>17. If and when your Fiero finally does break down for good, will you keep it or junk it?<BR>It will never be broken for long.  This is my last car.  Maybe I'll be buried in it.<P>||||reg||6
Z||000006||fiero56||05-09-2000||08:42 PM||||<BR>1. When did you start to like Fieros?<BR>About 3 years ago when I saw an Indy sitting in a parking lot beside the street.<BR>2. Why did you like them?<BR>They look like nothing else. The history of these cars just makes them that much more awsome.<BR>3. When and where did you first obtain your first Fiero?<BR>I bought mine from a guy about 30 minutes North of me.<BR>4. What type of Fiero do you own?<BR>1988 Formula(v-6) 5-speed.<BR>5. What year and model do you like the best?<BR>1988 Formula 5-speed.<BR>6. Do you have a nice paint job on it?<BR>Yes.<BR>7. What does it run like?<BR>Like a top.<BR>8. Do you get "looks" when driving your Fiero?<BR>Absolutely.<BR>9. What sound system do you have in your Fiero?<BR>Stock AM/FM cassette.<BR>10. Do your relatives and friends like Fieros?<BR>Yes.<BR>11.  Your Fiero?<BR>They like mine the best.<BR>12. Why do you think they cancelled the car (short answer please)?<BR>Many reasons. More than just one or two.<BR>13. Do you want a new Fiero to be released?<BR>No.<BR>14. If so, what would you want it to look like?<BR>NA.<BR>15. What plans do you have for your Fiero, in terms of upgrades, engine work, body kits, sound system, etc..<BR>Brakes, suspension, stereo.<BR>16. Do you think Fiero's will rise in collectors value?<BR>Some will.<BR>17. If and when your Fiero finally does break down for good, will you keep it or junk it?<BR>I will keep it. But the "when" part doesn't apply to me Fiero. It keeps going and going...<P>||||reg||1
Z||000007||zeusrekning||05-09-2000||08:59 PM||||Cliff is going to be pissed at the flames of over 1000 people replying Homicidal.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><BR> Sorry Cliff but hear i go.<P>1. When did you start to like Fieros?About 2 years ago when my dad bought one<BR>2. Why did you like them?look cool, rear engine,rides like sports car (I imagine)<BR>3. When and where did you first obtain your first Fiero?I traded my dad for my truck a bout a year ago<P>4. What type of Fiero do you own?87 coupe<P>5. What year and model do you like the best?87 gt i think<P>6. Do you have a nice paint job on it?<BR>It is ok but getting bad huge hole in fender from door falling<BR>7. What does it run like?Hell it's a fiero ran good this morning , don't know about tomorrow<P>8. Do you get "looks" when driving your Fiero?Yeah people usually get pissed cause i drve so slow<P>9. What sound system do you have in your Fiero?Just a cd player<P>10. Do your relatives and friends like Fieros?My dad does<P>11. Your Fiero?<P>12. Why do you think they cancelled the car (short answer please)?My dad says he thinks it is b/ of overheating and burning up<P>13. Do you want a new Fiero to be released?<BR>Yeah as long as i can afford it<BR>14. If so, what would you want it to look like?Mid engine Like the fastbacks but newer<P>15. What plans do you have for your Fiero, in terms of upgrades, engine work, body kits, sound system, etc..i plan on upgrading it,doing some engine work,body kit,sound system ect   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>16. Do you think Fiero's will rise in collectors value?hope so &lt;Can't go any lower can it<P>17. If and when your Fiero finally does break down for good, will you keep it or junk it?I did'nt<P><p>[This message has been edited by zeusrekning (edited 05-09-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000008||tgowens||05-09-2000||09:21 PM||||1. When did you start to like Fieros? <I>In 1992 when I first drove my girlfriend's silver '87 GT</I><P>2. Why did you like them? <I>They sound, look like and drive like no other car I have driven - I have had '55, '56 and '57 Chevys; '65 GTO, '55 and '57 T-Bird and even a '78 Datsun 280Z -- I restored them all but none are as much fun to drive as the Fiero.</I><P>3. When and where did you first obtain your first Fiero? <I>October 1999 from an individual in North Carolina</I><P>4. What type of Fiero do you own? <I>Gold 1987 GT (see  <A HREF="http://www.tgowens.com/fiero/" TARGET=_blank>www.tgowens.com/fiero/</A>  )</I><P>5. What year and model do you like the best? <I>1987 or 1988 GT</I><P>6. Do you have a nice paint job on it? <I>kinda sorta! -- the gold is fading and will be repainted very soon!</I><P>7. What does it run like? <I>I drove it from KY to CA and back and then from CA to KY and back for a total of around 10,000 miles and it ran fine!</I><P>8. Do you get "looks" when driving your Fiero? <I>Of course, don't you?</I><P>9. What sound system do you have in your Fiero? <I>Kenwood KDC-1011S AM/FM/CD with Pioneer front speakers (the only change I have made to a stock Fiero - hadda play cd's!! - oh yes, I did put on a Wolf bra - sheeesh, that wolf was HUGE - the bra is a size 87GT!!!</I><P>10. Do your relatives and friends like Fieros? <I>ubetcha!!</I><P>11. Your Fiero? <I>They'd better!!</I><P>12. Why do you think they cancelled the car (short answer please)? <I>cost-effectiveness of production in view of the changes in '88 as well as competition with the Corvette</I><P>13. Do you want a new Fiero to be released? <B>NO!!</B><P>14. If so, what would you want it to look like? <P>15. What plans do you have for your Fiero, in terms of upgrades, engine work, body kits, sound system, etc..  <I>new springs and shocks, new headliner, new paint and eventually a 3.4 swap, oh, and Mr. Mike's leather!</I><P>16. Do you think Fiero's will rise in collectors value? <I>Gee, I hope so but not until I get my '88 GT..........then it can go WAY up!!</I><P>17. If and when your Fiero finally does break down for good, will you keep it or junk it? <I>There is <B>no</B> breaking down - we keep replacing parts until it is new again.................</I>||||reg||1
Z||000009||frontal lobe||05-09-2000||10:20 PM||||Man, that's a lot of questions!!  I'll answer a few.<BR>1.  When did you start to like Fieros?  last fall<BR>2.  Why do you like them?  Relatively light weight.  Relatively rare.  Lots of conversion kits.<BR>3.  I got one last fall, then another this spring!<BR>4.  White '86GT and Maroon '87GT<BR>5.  I like the '86 and newer GT's best<BR>6.  White one oxidizing.  Maroon one is nice.<BR>7.  White one I blew the engine.  Maroon one runs nice.<BR>8.  If you ask my wife, yes, people looking and thinking how retarded it looks for a man of my age to be driving one.<BR>9.  Stock sound system with non-functioning tape player.  Sweet.  Driver's speaker sounds like it's cracked.<BR>10. Wife doesn't like the smell.  Kids think it's fun to ride in.  Don't have time for friends--I have 2 fieros (j/k).<BR>12.  Why did they cancel the car?  threat to corvette?<BR>13.  No new fiero please.  Keep ours vintage.<BR>14.  I really want to do the v8 conversion with a friend of mine.  Then put the 2.8 from the maroon one into the white one.<BR>16.  I don't see it being a collector, but you never know.<P>I guess I did wind up answering most of the questions.<P>||||reg||1
Z||000010||wkayl||05-09-2000||10:31 PM||||1. When did you start to like Fieros?<BR>1986 WHEN OUR COMPANY GAVE ONE AWAY<P>                 2. Why did you like them?<BR>LOOKED AND SOUNDED GREAT<P>                 3. When and where did you first obtain your first Fiero?<BR>MY SON'S 84 SE IN SEPT 1998<P>                 4. What type of Fiero do you own?<BR>I HAVE 86 GT AND MY SON NOW HAS 86 GT ALSO<P>                 5. What year and model do you like the best?<BR>86GT BUT I MAY BE BIASED. ACTUALLY ANY YEAR THAT YOU HAVE IS THE BEST<P>                 6. Do you have a nice paint job on it?<BR>MINE IS A GREAT ORIGINAL PAINT BUT MY SON'S CAR HAD A MACO JOB BEFORE HE GOT IT.  WE NEED TO WET SAND IT THIS SUMMER WHEN WE GET THE TIME AND THEN IT WILL BE GREAT ALSO.<P>                 7. What does it run like?<BR>SWEET<P>                 8. Do you get "looks" when driving your Fiero?<BR>THAT'S A GIVEN<P>                 9. What sound system do you have in your Fiero?<BR>AFTERMARKET CASSET WITH FACTORY SUB SYSTEM<P>                 10. Do your relatives and friends like Fieros?<BR>I GOT MINE FROM MY BROTHER'S MOTHER-IN-LAW.  THEY LIKE, MY DAD SAYS IT'S TOO SMALL.  MY WIFE IS DRIVING IT AS I'M TYPING THIS (SHE WENT SHOPPING).<P>                 11. Your Fiero? 1986.5 GT ALL ORIGINAL WITH 85,000 MILES<P>                 12. Why do you think they cancelled the car (short answer please)?<BR>THE SAME THING THAT HAPPENED TO STUDEBAKER, INTERNAL POWER STRUGGLES.<P>                 13. Do you want a new Fiero to be released?<BR>NO.  IT WOULD BE LIKE THE NEW MALABU, JUST A NAME TO SELL A CAR.<P>                 14. If so, what would you want it to look like?<BR>KINDA LIKE A SMALLER VERSION OF THE FIREBIRD ONLY MID ENGINE.<P>                 15. What plans do you have for your Fiero, in terms of upgrades, engine work, body kits,<BR>                 sound system, etc..<BR>NONE<P>                 16. Do you think Fiero's will rise in collectors value?<BR>YES LIKE THE '71 AAR CUDA I SOLD IN 76 FOR $800<P>                 17. If and when your Fiero finally does break down for good, will you keep it or junk it?<BR>IT WILL RUN FOREVER LIKE MY 61 STUDEBAKER I GOT IN '74 AND MY 67 BUICK SKYLARK CONV I GOT IN '76||||reg||1
Z||000011||Heisenhund||05-09-2000||10:36 PM||||1. When did you start to like Fieros?<BR>1985, when my brother-in-law bought one for my wife's sister. Of course, my wife had to have one, so I drove it. And started looking...<P>2. Why did you like them?<BR>It was small and low and stealthy and had more balls than it appeared to.<P>3. When and where did you first obtain your first Fiero?<BR>November 1985 at a used car lot. It was an 84 2M4.<P>4. What type of Fiero do you own?<BR>I am now the proud owner of an 86 GT.<P>5. What year and model do you like the best?<BR>Any year GT.<P>6. Do you have a nice paint job on it?<BR>The nicest factory paint job that's 14 years old.<P>7. What does it run like?<BR>Have you ever heard the phrase "Bat out of Hell"?<P>8. Do you get "looks" when driving your Fiero?<BR>Looks - always. The comments are what I like.."Is that one of them old Fiero cars?"<P>9. What sound system do you have in your Fiero?<BR>Sony AM/FM/Cassette with the factory sub.<P>10. Do your relatives and friends like Fieros?<BR>My wife does but she won't drive this one. I think she still feels responsible for wrecking my 84. She is, of course, but I told she could drive this one. As long as I'm in it. And it's a Sunday. Late at night. Under a full moon. In an empty parking lot.<P>11. Your Fiero?<BR>Damn Straight, it's my Fiero!<P>12. Why do you think they cancelled the car (short answer please)?<BR>Bad first year, the Firebird was losing ground & Pontiac needed to spend money on it.<P>13. Do you want a new Fiero to be released?<BR>Maybe something similar, but old cars should not be brought back (see VW Bug, Ford Festiva).<P>14. If so, what would you want it to look like?<BR>Like another car.<P>15. What plans do you have for your Fiero, in terms of upgrades, engine work, body kits, sound system, etc..<BR>Restore the sound system to factory, or at least have it to re-install later, same with engine & interior.<P>16. Do you think Fiero's will rise in collectors value?<BR>Definitely...the boom is coming.<P>17. If and when your Fiero finally does break down for good, will you keep it or junk it?<BR>Put all the restoration into it & put it away. Unless of course, the parking lot isn't completely empty when my wife drives it....<P>||||reg||1
Z||000012||LarryB||05-09-2000||10:39 PM||||<BR>1. When did you start to like Fieros?<BR>When I saw my first one up close in late 1983 while looking to buy my first new car.<P>2. Why did you like them?<BR>Because I really liked how they looked, because they were unique, and because you didn't have to sell your soul or have rich parents to own one, IIRC list price for base model was $7995.<P>3. When and where did you first obtain your first Fiero?<BR>1991, Wellesley MA.  It was the 2nd/fun car for the original owner, his business had been extremely successful and he decided he wanted to sell the Fiero and get a Corvette. His loss was my gain. :-)<P>4. What type of Fiero do you own?<BR>1986 Sport Coupe, 4 cyl 5 sp, Gold<BR>1986 SE, 6 cyl 4 sp, Gold<BR>1987 GT, 6 cyl 5 sp, Black<P>5. What year and model do you like the best?<BR>1986 SE.  If it had a Getrag it would be the perfect car as far as I'm concerned.<P>6. Do you have a nice paint job on it?<BR>All 3 cars have the original unfaded paint in good condition. The SE and GT each have 1 real blemish, neither of which I've tried to repair yet.<P>7. What does it run like?<BR>All are in excellent running condition.<BR>The SE and GT each have ~25K miles on them.<P>8. Do you get "looks" when driving your Fiero?<BR>Not that often, when I do its usually when I'm driving the SE.<P>9. What sound system do you have in your Fiero?<P>SC has a Kenwood CD unit with Pioneer 4x10s up front and Pioneer 4x6 plate speakers in the rear pillars, the SE has a Pioneer head with stock speakers, the GT has the stock Delco high end unit w/performance sound option.<P>10. Do your relatives and friends like Fieros?<BR>a few.  My mother even considered getting a new one at one point, she was in her 50's at the time.  If the trunk were bigger she probably would have gone for it. Ex-gf likes them as well, she bought an '85 GT a few months ago.<P>11.  Your Fiero?<P>My 30-something cousins and my 70+ yr old father sure do.<P>12. Why do you think they cancelled the car (short answer please)?<BR>2 reasons: 1) it was a niche market and GM was going to have to pay to continue to play and be competitive with the good cars coming out like MR2 & Miata 2) they didn't want more internal competition with their flagship Corvette (and to some extent Camaro/Firebird) <P>13. Do you want a new Fiero to be released?<P>No, at least not under that name, not with the abortions that GM comes up with now. To understand why, think of what a great car the original Mustang was, especially the 64-68 model cars, and then think of the Mustang II. Ugh. <P>If GM isn't going to do it right this time I just assume they corrupt some other name, and given their recent track record I have little confidence they would do it right. <P>14. If so, what would you want it to look like?<P>15. What plans do you have for your Fiero, in terms of upgrades, engine work, body kits, sound system, etc..<P>I will be removing and storing the stock seats in the SE and installing another set recovered with leather courtesy of Mr. Mike.<P>The GT is getting an undersized pulley and a Kevlar clutch in the very short term, exhaust manifolds cleaned up and reamed out (or maybe replaced with Sprints) sometime this summer, with a 3.4 swapout on the radar screen.<P>16. Do you think Fiero's will rise in collectors value?<P>The minty-condition lower mileage ones kept in good operating condition will.  IMO the ones with 100K+ miles on them won't, at least not for a very long time, regardless of the claims in some of the for-sale ads  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>17. If and when your Fiero finally does break down for good, will you keep it or junk it?<P>I can't keep unregistered cars on my property so if one breaks down for good it has to go, but I'd give someone else the opportunity to salvage it or reclaim parts they'd need, better it serve as a donor then be crushed.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000013||flexableface||05-09-2000||10:42 PM||||[QUOTE]Originally posted by Homicidal:<BR>[B]1. When did you start to like Fieros?<BR>last september<BR>2. Why did you like them?<BR>they are not an usuall car and the look bad a$$<BR>3. When and where did you first obtain your first Fiero?<BR>down the street in september<BR>4. What type of Fiero do you own?<BR>86 se<BR>5. What year and model do you like the best?<BR>86 gt<BR>6. Do you have a nice paint job on it?<BR>it orignal now but in good shape it will be repainted in the fall or sooner<BR>7. What does it run like?<BR>it runs pretty good <BR>8. Do you get "looks" when driving your Fiero?<BR>once in a while<BR>9. What sound system do you have in your Fiero?<BR>kenwood head unit pionier 4x10 and 4x6 and im runing a amp to the 4x10. and i got a bass light. <BR>10. Do your relatives and friends like Fieros?<BR>some of them do <BR>11.  Your Fiero?<BR>a few of my friends do<BR>12. Why do you think they cancelled the car (short answer please)?<BR>you got me there<BR>13. Do you want a new Fiero to be released?<BR>why not<BR>14. If so, what would you want it to look like?<BR>a lot like the gts<BR>15. What plans do you have for your Fiero, in terms of upgrades, engine work, body kits, sound system, etc..<BR>rebuilt 2.8, cam, port and polish heads and intake, biger bore throttle body, better injectors, beefed up trans, shift kit, and hopefully a turbo, ram air, side scoop, rims,rear deck lid scoop. <BR>16. Do you think Fiero's will rise in collectors value?<BR>i  think they will<BR>17. If and when your Fiero finally does break down for good, will you keep it or junk it/ it will keep it as long as i possiblely can.<P>||||reg||1
Z||000014||stimpy||05-09-2000||11:24 PM||||Here goes...<P>1. Always liked the looks, especially after the 86 GT came out, but believed the (negative) hype. My dad bought a red 86 GT in 96 and I just fell in love with it. I was amazed I could actually fit in it!<P>2. cuz they look so good! Plus the safety qualties, good looks, performance potential, good looks, relative abundance of parts for a semi-exotic car, good looks, and mid engined handling. I also think they look kind cool.<P>3. August of 98, private party seller in Stockton, CA. Took all of 5 minutes to realize it was worth every dime of the $2500 I paid.<P>4. 86 GT, gold, no wing, luggage rack, factory leather, sunroof, pw,pl<P>5. Fastback GT.. any year. close 2nd would be an 85 2M6 SE, 3rd Formula<P>6 Adequate factory paint. Gold is a beautiful color, but it does have a tendency to fade. Looks almost silver in areas.<P>7. Runs better then new. Freshly rebuilt motor with .030 over-bore,forged pistons, crank and rods, Accel super coil & 8mm wires, Bosch Platinum plugs. Revs quick & smooth.<P>8. I guess so. Everyone down here has tinted windows, so it's hard to tell.<BR>Kds on their bikes seem to think it's cool.<P>9. Sony CD player, Jensen Coax Front & Rear, Aura Pro Sies Bass Shakers under the seat. Plenty of shake & boom inside, whisper quiet on the outside. I don't like to advertise. <P>10 Family- yes, my parents are Fiero nuts (my dad has a s/c 3.8 in his GT, my mom lets him) My niece likes to ride in it. My brother has a Camaro, but we love him anyway. Friends put up with me yabbering about it.<P>11. ?<P>12. Cuz they are stupid poopy-heads!<P>13. I wouldn't be able to afford one, but I think it would be very cool to have a mid-engined Saturn sports car with the V6 out of the LS, S/C 3.8 for a GT version. No more Fieros though.<P>14. The car above... Saturn SC styling on Fiero proportions, but a bit larger (not much)<P>15. Hehehe... Mrs. Stimpy is not around, so the truth can be known!  Monochromatic Lexus gold paint job, 16" rims, coilovers, 1.5" drop front, 2" drop rear, rear swaybar, Design1 turbo kit... so many plans, so few bonus checks.<P>16. Probably, but I really don't care, I don't plan on ever parting with mine. Rather they stay cheap and our little secret.<P>17. Break down for good? What the hell does that mean? Never say die! <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000015||Raydar||05-09-2000||11:26 PM||||1. When did you start to like Fieros?<BR>The first time I saw one. Especially when the first GT came out, with the Pace Car bodywork.<P>2. Why did you like them?<BR>Looks (with Aero bodywork), V-6 rumble.<BR>also the plastic body panels.<P>3. When and where did you first obtain your first Fiero?<BR>Spring 1985. Baranco Pontiac in Decatur GA<BR>(New 85 GT)<P>4. What type of Fiero do you own?<BR>88 red Formula. T-top. 88 red coupe. Both automatic.<P>5. What year and model do you like the best?<BR>88 Formula. 85 GT. 86-87 SE.<P>6. Do you have a nice paint job on it?<BR>Faded. Have plans in the works...<P>7. What does it run like?<BR>Great!<P>8. Do you get "looks" when driving your Fiero?<BR>Occasionally. Most folks out here don't care too much. Everybody drives a Ford truck.<P>9. What sound system do you have in your Fiero?<BR>Delco cassette with EQ and touchpad controls. Pioneer 4X10s in the dash. Soon to be upgraded to CD.<P>10. Do your relatives and friends like Fieros?<BR>Mostly just the guys in the club. GA Fieros.<P>11. Your Fiero?<BR>Wife hates it.<P>12. Why do you think they cancelled the car (short answer please)?<BR>By 1990-91, it was "gonna put the Corvette on the trailer."<P>13. Do you want a new Fiero to be released?<BR>Sure. Why not...<P>14. If so, what would you want it to look like?<BR>Could use the same basic chassis as the 88. Possibly a body that is styled like the Firebird.<BR>PLEASE, NO SLATS like the Grand Am. Sheesh!<BR>3.4 and 3800 engine.<P>15. What plans do you have for your Fiero, in terms of upgrades, engine work, body kits, sound system, etc..<BR>3.4 swap. Maybe some different wheels. IRM decklid spoiler. Godzilla sound system.<BR>Bright *metallic* red paint.<P>16. Do you think Fiero's will rise in collectors value?<BR>Anybody's guess.<BR>(What are Corvairs doing, these days? Very similar situation.)<P>17. If and when your Fiero finally does break down for good, will you keep it or junk it? <BR>Only way it's gonna be "junked" is if it gets severely wadded up. Otherwise, I'm going to keep fixing it. If it gets too bent to repair, then I'll part it out. Only when it's an empty hull will it go to the crusher.<P>||||reg||1
Z||000016||Racer 1||05-09-2000||11:28 PM||||1. When did you start to like Fieros? 1989 when I saw a Black 88 GT. The car was a sleeper.<P>2. Why did you like them? Plastic body panels and parts are easy to get and cheap.<P>3. When and where did you first obtain your first Fiero? At a cheesy used car dealer in 1992-1993 I cant remeber the year now.<P>4. What type of Fiero do you own? 1986 coupe with the <B>DUCK</B><P>5. What year and model do you like the best? All except I hated my friends 85 coupe with 4 speed manual tranny. I hate the brown interior.<P>6. Do you have a nice paint job on it?<BR>Yes! I painted the car myself almost.<P>7. What does it run like? My car runs like a 1986 FIERO 2.5 <P>8. Do you get "looks" when driving your Fiero? Of course I love reving my engine when I pass cute ladies walking outside. And if they have a nice azz and a big rack I give them honk.<P>9. What sound system do you have in your Fiero? Kenwood excelon tape deck with 10 cd cahnger.Two bazooka 8" subs 1 fosgate 200dsm amp for the bass 1 rockford fosgate 40dsm for the mids and a coustic amp for the tweeters. And a coustic xm-5 for the crossover with bass control.<P>10. Do your relatives and friends like Fieros?<BR>Yes in a way.<BR>11. Your Fiero?<P>12. Why do you think they cancelled the car (short answer please)? Because the fiero  would have been better then the corvette.<P>13. Do you want a new Fiero to be released?<BR>!!!! NO !!!!!<BR>14. If so, what would you want it to look like?<P>15. What plans do you have for your Fiero, in terms of upgrades, engine work, body kits, sound system, etc.. Quad-4 HO next year and bigger brakes.<P>16. Do you think Fiero's will rise in collectors value? I really dont know. Kinda hope not so I can get a 88 GT for cheap.<P>17. If and when your Fiero finally does break down for good, will you keep it or junk it?<BR>Im going to be buried in my fiero!<BR>||||reg||3
Z||000017||WisconsinGT||05-09-2000||11:34 PM||||1. When did you start to like Fieros? <BR>In 1988<P>                       <BR>2. Why did you like them?<BR>Style, Price<P>                       <BR>3. When and where did you first obtain your first Fiero?<BR>In 1988 off the showroom floor of the local Pontiac dealer.<P>                       <BR>4. What type of Fiero do you own? <BR>1988GT<P>                       <BR>5. What year and model do you like the best?<BR>1988GT<P>                       <BR>6. Do you have a nice paint job on it?<BR>No!<P>                       <BR>7. What does it run like?<BR>Runs like a 12 year old car.<P>                       <BR>8. Do you get "looks" when driving your Fiero?<BR>All the time.<P>                       <BR>9. What sound system do you have in your Fiero?<BR>Stock AC Delco Am/FM W/Equalizer<P>                       <BR>10. Do your relatives and friends like Fieros?<BR>I guess<P>                       <BR>11. Your Fiero? <BR>Alot of people laugh. If they only had a brain!<P>                       <BR>12. Why do you think they cancelled the car (short answer please)?<BR>Reputation<P>                       <BR>13. Do you want a new Fiero to be released?<BR>No!<P>                       <BR>14. If so, what would you want it to look like?<P>                       <BR>15. What plans do you have for your Fiero, in terms of upgrades, engine work, body kits,<BR>sound system, etc.<BR>3.4, New paint, Rims.<P>                       <BR>16. Do you think Fiero's will rise in collectors value?<BR>Most certainly.<P>                       <BR>17. If and when your Fiero finally does break down for good, will you keep it or junk it?<BR>Ahh, that will never happen.||||reg||1
Z||000018||FieroGTGirl||05-10-2000||01:37 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Homicidal:<BR><B>1. When did you start to like Fieros?<BR>       1995...When my Geo Metro died...<BR>2. Why did you like them?<BR>       Sporty & Fun<BR>3. When and where did you first obtain your first Fiero?<BR>       1995~~at Hyatt Pontiac in Tacoma<BR>4. What type of Fiero do you own?<BR>       First one 86 SE, Current 86 GT<BR>5. What year and model do you like the best?<BR>       1986 GT<BR>6. Do you have a nice paint job on it?<BR>        I WISH!!!!<BR>7. What does it run like?<BR>      RUNS GREAT!!!<BR>8. Do you get "looks" when driving your Fiero?<BR>      OF course!! <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><BR>9. What sound system do you have in your Fiero?<BR>      Stock with bad right/front speaker(going to upgrade stereo soon anyway)<BR>10. Do your relatives and friends like Fieros?<BR>       they are UNimpressed<BR>11.  Your Fiero?<BR>       Yeah, they just hate to sit in it...everyone complains how low it is.<BR>12. Why do you think they cancelled the car (short answer please)?<BR>       because of BAD rap<BR>13. Do you want a new Fiero to be released?<BR>      NO, keep it rare!<BR>14. If so, what would you want it to look like?<P>15. What plans do you have for your Fiero, in terms of upgrades, engine work, body kits, sound system, etc..<BR>     All I know is I want a LOUD stereo and a FASTER car.....<BR>16. Do you think Fiero's will rise in collectors value?<BR>      OH YEAH!<BR>17. If and when your Fiero finally does break down for good, will you keep it or junk it?</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><BR>    KEEP IT....I am a FIERO ADDICT NOW!!<BR>||||reg||10
Z||000019||Haze_Performance||05-10-2000||01:47 AM||||1. When did you start to like Fieros?<BR>AN:High School<P>2. Why did you like them?<BR>AN:Cool looking cars<P>3. When and where did you first obtain your first Fiero? AN:7 Months ago,Buddy works at a Dealer<P>4. What type of Fiero do you own? AN:1985 2M4<P>5. What year and model do you like the best? AN:1984 to 1988 2M4/2M6/SE/Formula/GT/INDY<P>6. Do you have a nice paint job on it? AN:Great Paint<P>7. What does it run like? AN:A BRAND NEW Car<P>8. Do you get "looks" when driving your Fiero? AN:YES<P>9. What sound system do you have in your Fiero? AN:CD Player/New Speakers/soon to have a 10" Sub<P>10. Do your relatives and friends like Fieros? AN: Love it<P>11. Your Fiero? AN:See Above<P>12. Why do you think they cancelled the car (short answer please)?AN:Not a large market for this kind of car at the time<P>13. Do you want a new Fiero to be released? AN:NO....They would never be the same<P>14. If so, what would you want it to look like? AN:See Above<P>15. What plans do you have for your Fiero, in terms of upgrades, engine work, body kits, sound system, etc..AN: Side scoops,Ram Air T/A hood scoop,2000 Pontiac Grand Am GT Chrome 16" 5 star wheels,Chevy 350,+ much more<P>16. Do you think Fiero's will rise in collectors value? AN:Over Time<P>17. If and when your Fiero finally does break down for good, will you keep it or junk it? AN: Fieros NEVER break down for good...some people just give up on them.NOT ME!! <P>||||reg||10
