Z||000021||fierodave||05-10-2000||03:28 AM||||1. When did you start to like Fieros?<BR>4 YEARS AGO<BR>2. Why did you like them?<BR>LOOKED GOOD<BR>3. When and where did you first obtain your first Fiero?<BR>4 YEARS FROM A FRIEND<BR>4. What type of Fiero do you own?<BR>2 86 GT'S 1 INDY  1 84 COUPE<BR>5. What year and model do you like<BR>the best?  86-88GT THEN THE INDY<BR>6. Do you have a nice paint job on<BR> it?  INDY HAS A NEW ONE  WHITE 86 IS MINT<BR>7. What does it run like?<BR>ALL RUN PERFECT!<BR>8. Do you get "looks" when driving<BR> your Fiero? THERE HEAD TURNERS<BR>9. What sound system do you have in your Fiero? STOCK<BR>10. Do your relatives and friends like Fieros? YEP THEY HAVE TOO LOL<BR>11. Your Fiero? YES SIR<BR>12. Why do you think they cancelled the car (short answer please)?<BR>COMPANY (GM) POLITIC'S<BR>13. Do you want a new Fiero to be released? HELL NO<BR>14. If so, what would you want it to look like? SEE ABOVE<BR>15. What plans do you have for your Fiero, in terms of upgrades, engine work, body kits, sound system, etc..<BR>MAY INSTALL REMOTE LOCKS SO I DON'T HAVE TO KEEP TRACK OF SO MANY KEYS LOL KEEP THEM STOCK WORTH MORE DOWN THE ROAD IN THREE OR 4 YEARS.<BR>16. Do you think Fiero's will rise in collectors value? SEE ABOVE  LOL<BR>17. If and when your Fiero finally does break down for good, will you keep it or junk it? NEVER HAPPEN<P><p>[This message has been edited by fierodave (edited 05-10-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000022||lennyb4||05-10-2000||08:59 AM||||1. When did you start to like Fieros?<BR>A. About three years ago when i got my first    one.<P>2. Why did you like them?<BR>A. Fast, sleek, sporty, and just a hole lot     of fun to drive.<P>3. When and where did you first obtain your     first Fiero?<BR>A. 1997 I bought it from my drill sargent in    Texas when i was in the service.<P>4. What type of Fiero do you own?<BR>A. Currently i own three a 1987 GT, 1987    Coupe, and a 1986 GT.<P>5. What year and model do you like the best?<BR>A. I like all fiero's between 1986 - 1988.<P>6. Do you have a nice paint job on it?<BR>A. Both GT's are mint, 87 Coupe is nice but i    want to repaint (spiderwebbing on rear).<P>7. What does it run like?<BR>A. GT's are both missing motors, 87 Coupoe    runs like a dream.(alot of work to get it    there  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>8. Do you get "looks" when driving your    Fiero?<BR>A. I love it when people try to figure out    what kind of car it is.<P>9. What sound system do you have in your    Fiero?<BR>A. All three are factory AM/FM cassette.<P>10. Do your relatives and friends like     Fieros?<BR>A.  I think my wife gets alittle jeolous now     and then. As for other people i really     dont care. I love them and thats what     counts.<P>11. Your Fiero?<BR>A.  See answer above.<P>12. Why do you think they cancelled the car     (short answer please)?<BR>A.  Well i believe the fiero was becoming so     popular that it was hurting their     corvette sales. A sporty car that cost     1/3 the price..<P>13. Do you want a new Fiero to be released?<BR>A.  Actually, NO.. I like the idea that we     are a special class of car lovers. Not     every one would put the time into a 12-15     year old car like alot of us do.<P>14. If so, what would you want it to look     like?<P>15. What plans do you have for your Fiero, in     terms of upgrades, engine work, body<BR>    kits, sound system, etc..<BR>A.  87 GT is going to get a 305 out of a 94     Camaro. 87 Coupe is getting a 3800 turbo.<BR>    I already have both motors, now just     waiting for the money to start on them.<P>16. Do you think Fiero's will rise in     collectors value?<BR>A.  As long as they dont bring it back i know     it will.<P>17. If and when your Fiero finally does break     down for good, will you keep it or junk     it?<BR>A.  Just call me doctor frankinstien. It     shall live again..HAHAHAHAHAHA<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000023||ChadMan||05-10-2000||09:22 AM||||1. When did you start to like Fieros? <I>1983, when I first saw one at a Pontiac manufacturer's tent at Mid-Ohio.  I was 12 years old</I><P>2. Why did you like them? <I>I thought that first Fiero was the most beautiful car I'd ever seen that wasn't made in Maranello, Italy</I><P>3. When and where did you first obtain your first Fiero? <I>1992 - bought a red 84 Coupe from a retired AF pilot in Westerville, OH</I><P>4. What type of Fiero do you own? <I>88 Coupe, 5-sp. Formerly owned 84 4-sp Coupe and 86 4-sp V6 SE</I><P>5. What year and model do you like the best? I love them all: <I>GT's, SE's, Formulas, Indys, Coupes - even the 84 in our parking lot with chalked paint, a bad tint job and headlights stuck open</I><P>6. Do you have a nice paint job on it? <I>Except for two spots that are starting to fade, yes</I><P>7. What does it run like? <I>Runs great, handles great (KYB shocks/struts and Formula springs out back), stops on a dime</I><P>8. Do you get "looks" when driving your Fiero?  <I>I did in the SE (red w/wing), but no one seems to notice my Coupe unless I'm passing them at 85 mph or so</I><P>9. What sound system do you have in your Fiero?  <I>Blaupunkt CD w/Pyle 4x10's</I><P>10. Do your relatives and friends like Fieros?  <I>They do now!</I><P>11. Your Fiero?  <I>Yep!  My wife wishes mine had A/C though</I><P>12. Why do you think they cancelled the car (short answer please)?  <I>Too many 2-seaters sold from 1983-1988, high insurance rates</I><P>13. Do you want a new Fiero to be released?  <I>Yes</I><P>14. If so, what would you want it to look like?  <I>A lot like the original</I><P>15. What plans do you have for your Fiero, in terms of upgrades, engine work, body kits, sound system, etc.  <I>If I don't buy a GT soon, I plan to have Ed Parks install a Camaro 3.4 in my Coupe</I><P>16. Do you think Fiero's will rise in collectors value?  <I>Yes, but not very far - they'll always be affordable, like Corvairs</I><P>17. If and when your Fiero finally does break down for good, will you keep it or junk it?  <I>Unless the frame is bent or rusted beyond repair, a Fiero is incapable of breaking down for good!</I><P><p>[This message has been edited by ChadMan (edited 05-10-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000024||Oreif||05-10-2000||09:24 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Homicidal:<BR><B>1. When did you start to like Fieros?<BR>1984, When I first saw the Indy Fiero<BR>2. Why did you like them?<BR>They looked great!<BR>3. When and where did you first obtain your first Fiero?<BR>1986 bought a black SE right from dealer!<BR>4. What type of Fiero do you own?<BR>1986 SE Black (not the one originally purchased above)<BR>5. What year and model do you like the best?<BR>84 Indy, 86 SE, 88 GT<BR>6. Do you have a nice paint job on it?<BR>90% is orginal paint, Hand Buffed<BR>7. What does it run like?<BR>It runs very well!<BR>8. Do you get "looks" when driving your Fiero? Yes often.<P>9. What sound system do you have in your Fiero? AM/FM/CD with a powered sub (aftermarket)<P>10. Do your relatives and friends like Fieros? Some do.<P>11.  Your Fiero? Yes<P>12. Why do you think they cancelled the car (short answer please)?<BR>GM corporate didn't like the fact the employees owned factory so they killed it to make the mini-vans.<BR>13. Do you want a new Fiero to be released?<BR>No.<BR>14. If so, what would you want it to look like?<P>15. What plans do you have for your Fiero, in terms of upgrades, engine work, body kits, sound system, etc..<BR>Going to do an engine swap in the future, Haven't decided on engine.<BR>16. Do you think Fiero's will rise in collectors value?<BR>Hey even the edsel was called a flop and they still ar worth large amounts of money!<P>17. If and when your Fiero finally does break down for good, will you keep it or junk it?</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE> <BR>They can break down for good? Unless some fool hits me and totals it I'm taking it to the grave!<P>||||reg||1
Z||000025||Fformula88||05-10-2000||09:43 AM||||1. When my dad bought an 87 coupe in 1990.  He still has it too!  I was 13.<P>2.  I thought it was just a really cool looking sports car.  <P>3.  I bought my Fiero in June 1996, from a used car lot.  67K miles for $2850<P>4.  Its a 1988 Fiero Formula, only 5,484 of them!<P>5.  The year and model I own.  The GT mechanicals in the coupe body make for a real sleeper!  The GT fastbacks are cool too... I like them all.<P>6.  The paint is in GREAT shape... bright red with only a few scratches and no bad spots.  <P>7.  It runs good, except for the mysterious V6 erratic idle problem.<P>8.  I get a lot of looks in my Fiero, but my favorite is when I have the back open, and people are surprised the engine is in the back!<P>9.  I have an Alpine CD deck, and a set of JBL 4X10's in the dash.  Soon to replace the 4X6's in the sail panels<P>10.  My dad's a big Fiero fan, and owns his own Fiero.  My Mother cannot get in or out of them, so she hates them.<P>11.  My friends love my Fiero, calling it a Ferraro (combination of Fiero and Ferrari).  They are always trying to buy it off of my.<P>12.  Due to mismanagement, and lack of support at the top that caused the mismanagement, GM let the car become unprofitable giving it a reason to pull the plug.<P>13.  I would love to see a new Fiero released, but only if it was a similar car... 2 seats, mid engine sports car, preferrable with a convertable version.<P>14.  I think it should look like an evolution of the Fiero design.  Not a ripoff of another car's design (like the MR2 Spyder--- Boxster)<P>15.  I would like to put a 3.4L into my Fiero, but in the near future I would like to upgrade the headers and exhaust, and get some 4X6 speakers.  <P>16.  I think '88 GT's have a good chance of rising in collecters value.  They are considered the newest, and most rare with their redesigned suspensions.<P>17.  I'll replace parts to keep it going until it is impossible.  If I have a BIG garage to keep it, I would, but practically if it was NEVER going to be driveable again, I'd probably get rid of it.  Cars are meant to be driven!<P>17.  ||||reg||10
Z||000026||LAMBO||05-10-2000||09:55 AM||||1. When did you start to like Fieros? <BR>I've liked them since they were first introduced by Pontiac.<BR>2. Why did you like them?<BR>Inexpensive mid-engine fun, not to mention good looking.<P>3. When and where did you first obtain your first Fiero? But it from a friend for $500.<P>4. What type of Fiero do you own?<BR>1985 2m6 SE<P>5. What year and model do you like the best?<BR>'86 or'87 GTs<P>6. Do you have a nice paint job on it?<BR>Not yet, but it will be soon.<P>7. What does it run like? Runs strong, erratic idle when cold, needs new exhaust.<P>8. Do you get "looks" when driving your Fiero? Don't know, haven't driven it much yet.<P>9. What sound system do you have in your Fiero?<BR>None at the moment, its sitting in a box.<P>10. Do your relatives and friends like Fieros? Not really.<P>11. Your Fiero? To soon to tell.<P>12. Why do you think they cancelled the car (short answer please)? Bad press. Saturn.<P>13. Do you want a new Fiero to be released? If it looked good and performed well, you bet.<P>14. If so, what would you want it to look like? Take some styling tips from the Finale rebody kit.<P>15. What plans do you have for your Fiero, in terms of upgrades, engine work, body kits, sound system, etc..<BR>Small block Chevy, Complete suspension upgrade, New nose, 16" alloys with treads, brand new paint.<P>16. Do you think Fiero's will rise in collectors value? Formulas, Indy's, 88 GT, maybe.<P>17. If and when your Fiero finally does break down for good, will you keep it or junk it? I won't ever let that happen.<P>||||reg||1
Z||000027||TheFiero64||05-10-2000||10:53 AM||||1. <B>When did you start to like Fieros?</B><BR>About 5 years ago<P>2. <B>Why did you like them?</B><BR>look feel and just about everything else about them<P>3. <B>When and where did you first obtain your first Fiero?</B><BR>2 1/2 years ago in a salvage yard. It was in great shape and someone didn't think it was worth it to replace a broken clutch.<P>4. <B>What type of Fiero do you own?</B><BR><UL TYPE=SQUARE><BR><LI> 84 red SE(<I>it is actually my girls but I call it mine</I>)<BR><LI> 86 red GT<BR><LI> 86 SE parts car<BR><LI> 88 red coupe v6 <BR></UL><BR>5. <B>What year and model do you like the best?</B><BR>88 GT<P>6. <B>Do you have a nice paint job on it?</B><BR>not yet<P>7. <B>What does it run like?</B><BR>all but the parts car & GT run great. The GT will when it gets an engine<P>8. <B>Do you get "looks" when driving your Fiero?</B><BR>Sometimes<P>9. <B>What sound system do you have in your Fiero?</B><BR>A GM cd player that looks stock<P>10. <B>Do your relatives and friends like Fieros?</B><BR>Yes<P>11. <B>Your Fiero?</B><BR>Yes<P>12. <B>Why do you think they canceled the car (short answer please)?</B><BR>thought they would lose too much money<P>13. <B>Do you want a new Fiero to be released?</B><BR>yes and no<P>14. <B>If so, what would you want it to look like?</B><BR>the 88 GT with a few upgrades. <I>I don't think they should make it that different.</I><P>15. <B>What plans do you have for your Fiero, in terms of upgrades, engine work, body kits, sound system, etc..</B><BR>Lots always.<P>16. <B>Do you think Fiero's will rise in collectors value?</B><BR>Yes<P>17. <B>If and when your Fiero finally does break down for good, will you keep it or junk it?</B> I would not let it get that broke!<P>||||reg||10
Z||000028||Monkeyman||05-10-2000||11:58 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Homicidal:<BR><B>1. When did you start to like Fieros?<BR>     When I saw my first one.  Detroit Auto Show in '82 or '83.<P>2. Why did you like them?<BR>    What's not to like?<P>3. When and where did you first obtain your first Fiero?<BR>     Last fall.  My wife found it for me in Ohio.<BR>     <BR>4. What type of Fiero do you own?<BR>     '86 SC (Monkeymobile-parts car) and '85 GT (Grape Ape)<P>5. What year and model do you like the best?<BR>     '85 GT<P>6. Do you have a nice paint job on it?<BR>     Pearlized-mostly purple.  Needs repainted, but looks very unique.<P>7. What does it run like?<BR>     Currently it's up on a rack at the local garage getting another motor installed.  I'll let you know this weekend.<P>8. Do you get "looks" when driving your Fiero?<BR>     I sure did when the Monkeymobile was on the road!  And it's "just" a base model.<P>9. What sound system do you have in your Fiero?<BR>     Currently nothing, but I plan on a mid to high end set up.  Probably a good cassette head unit, 5 1/4" separates (custom mounted in the dash), 8" sub,  CD changer, a couple of amps, etc.<P>10. Do your relatives and friends like Fieros?<BR>     My kid thinks it's cool.  My wife [b]claims</B> not to like it, but...<P>11.  Your Fiero?<BR>     Don't understand the question.<P>12. Why do you think they cancelled the car (short answer please)?<BR>     Competition with the Vette and the damn beancounters.<P>13. Do you want a new Fiero to be released?<BR>     NO!<P>14. If so, what would you want it to look like?<P>15. What plans do you have for your Fiero, in terms of upgrades, engine work, body kits, sound system, etc..<BR>     Lowering springs, poly bushings, tinted windows, taller wing stands, either a 3800SC or a V8 (eventually),  no muffler, aftermarket seats (should be on the way)<P>16. Do you think Fiero's will rise in collectors value?<BR>     Not much.  Bad for the collector, good for me.<P>17. If and when your Fiero finally does break down for good, will you keep it or junk it?<BR>     Keep it of course.  This has already happened and the Monkeymobile is still sitting in my driveway.[/B]<HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>||||reg||1
Z||000029||Gold-86SE||05-10-2000||12:10 PM||||1. When did you start to like Fieros?<P>1988, I was a Junior in High School.<P>2. Why did you like them?<P>Had speakers in the seat, and a real boom on the bass, also small and sporty for a 4-cyl 4-spd.<P>3. When and where did you first obtain your first Fiero?<P>Which one, the ones that did not run or the one that runs. The first one that did not run, about 1995 (now a parts car), the one that runs January 2000. Waited 12 long years to get my Gold SE and she's my baby.<P>4. What type of Fiero do you own?<P>1986 Gold SE V6 4-spd, AC PL PW PM, Cruise Control, Premium Sound (stock sub-woofer) Rear Defrost, Trunk Release, Sunroof, Spoiler, 215 60 14s sittin' on the original gold alloys (nothing looks finer).<P>5. What year and model do you like the best?<P>Any Notch Back, never have liked the FBs.<P>6. Do you have a nice paint job on it?<P>Pretty Nice for being the original paint, yet there is a little fade on the spoiler and nose.<P>7. What does it run like?<P>Like a champ, and begs to be driven fast.<P>8. Do you get "looks" when driving your Fiero?<P>Have had several waves from fellow fiero owners, but not much from other drivers. Yet, have had several challenges from Mustangs, and F-bodies.  Most looks come from pedestrians who almost fall over their feet trying to break their neck getting a better look at the fiero.<P>9. What sound system do you have in your Fiero?<P>Stock. And don't want it any other way, I prefer the music from the engine.<P>10. Do your relatives and friends like Fieros?<P>My family likes them, my Father-in-law hates all fieros and mine in particular. My FIL thinks I sold out my dream of owning a 'vette for a Fiero. I used to like 'vette until I learned better. Who wants a bulky fat 'vette anyway?<P>11. Your Fiero?<P>See answer 10.<P>12. Why do you think they cancelled the car (short answer please)?<P>Don't get me started. My thoughts summarized in two words: "Conspiracy Theory."<P>13. Do you want a new Fiero to be released?<P>Most defiantly(sp) but the current Fiero will show it age depending on how any future fiero/son of fiero is release.<P>14. If so, what would you want it to look like?<P>Would like it to resemble the fiero, but take the passing of time into consideration. Possibly making it something that it might have been, had fiero production never ceased.<P>15. What plans do you have for your Fiero, in terms of upgrades, engine work, body kits, sound system, etc...?<P>Better exhaust, poly bushings all around, short shifter, modified suspension, that's pretty much it, oh... and the most important, replacing everything that breaks - because it is sure to fail. Forget rebodies, body kits bastardize the fiero concept. It is impossible to make the fiero something is it not (i.e. Lambo). It is too good looking as it sets to mess it up.<P>16. Do you think Fiero's will rise in collectors value?<P>Original fieros with low miles, will bring the most money. But hey, I buy a car to drive and have fun, not to have it sit in the freaking garage like some trophy.<P>17. If and when your Fiero finally does break down for good, will you keep it or junk it?<P>As of today, it will not break down for good, because it is babied and maintained. Anything that fails will be replaced or repaired so that my fiero may "live long and prosper" - a little spock lingo there.<p>[This message has been edited by Gold-86SE (edited 05-10-2000).]||||reg||6
Z||000030||RiceCooker||05-10-2000||02:45 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR><BR><B>1. When did you start to like Fieros? ...mmmmmm.... Fieros <P>2. Why did you like them? ...mmmmmm.... Fieros <P>3. When and where did you first obtain your first Fiero? ...mmmmmm.... Fieros <P>4. What type of Fiero do you own? ...mmmmmm.... Fieros <P>5. What year and model do you like the best? ...mmmmmm.... Fieros <P>6. Do you have a nice paint job on it? ...mmmmmm.... Fieros <P>7. What does it run like? ...mmmmmm.... Fieros <P>8. Do you get "looks" when driving your Fiero? ...mmmmmm.... Fieros <P>9. What sound system do you have in your Fiero? ...mmmmmm.... Fieros <P>10. Do your relatives and friends like Fieros? ...mmmmmm.... Fieros <P>11.  Your Fiero? ...mmmmmm.... Fieros <P>12. Why do you think they cancelled the car (short answer please)? .m. Fieros <BR>13. Do you want a new Fiero to be released? ...mmmmmm.... Fieros <P>14. If so, what would you want it to look like? ...mmmmmm.... Fieros <P>15. What plans do you have for your Fiero, in terms of upgrades, engine work, body kits, sound system, etc.. ...mmmmmm.... Fieros <P>16. Do you think Fiero's will rise in collectors value? ...mmmmmm.... Fieros <P>17. If and when your Fiero finally does break down for good, will you keep it or junk it? ...mmmmmm.... Fieros <BR>....Huh?....What?....Survey?....where?....<BR>I didn't see any surv...mmmmmm.... fieros<P><BR></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>||||reg||7
Z||000031||RobertVol||05-10-2000||03:00 PM||||When did you start to like Fieros - I started when I was 16 it was my first car ....87 Blue GT. LOVED it<P>2.Why do you like them?  uh Have youe ever drove one?!?!? plus looks of GT...nothing looks like it one the road..<P>3.When and were did I obtain 1st fiero - See #1 was purchased @Coggin Pontiac in Jacksonville<P>4.What type of fiero do you own? - <BR>1988 GT White 54k miles GEN II 3800 SC 5 speed<P>1988 GT White ttops 55kmiles stock <P>1988 GT Stock 28k milesgetting ready to do conversion - justhought I would put more miles on it before wasting this low mileage motor<P>5.What year and model do you like the best? Uh 87-88 GT especially with t tops on the 88<P>6. Do you have a nice paint job/<BR>YES ! On all three mint condition. <BR>(i was lucky one was fixed after that @#$@!@#!@!# SUV ran over the front of it!!!Great body work was done<P>7. What does it run like/<BR>Vmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmm!<BR>Vmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmm!<BR>Vmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmm!<BR>(Switch gear)<BR>VmmmmmmmVmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmVmmmmmmmmm!<P>8. Do you get looks when driving your fiero/<BR>yes but especially when the t topsare out of my  t topper<P>9.What sound system do you have in your fiero/<BR>Stock in 2 and Pioneer Factory size replacment CD payer in the other. it looks great in the spot.<P>10. Do your relatives and friends like Fieros?<BR>Who cares ....I do ||||reg||1
Z||000032||Coconut||05-10-2000||10:39 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Homicidal:<BR><B>1. When did you start to like Fieros?<BR>Ever since Pontiac first introduced them.<BR>2. Why did you like them?<BR>Finally,a 2-seat sports car even I could afford (eventually)....and the "Look"... <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/cool.gif"><BR>3. When and where did you first obtain your first Fiero?<BR>'92 or '93<BR>4. What type of Fiero do you own?<BR>'86 GT<BR>5. What year and model do you like the best?<BR>'86-'88 GT<BR>6. Do you have a nice paint job on it?<BR>A BEAUTIFUL deep,dark,metallic forest green......and then the alarm woke me up  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><BR>7. What does it run like?<BR>Solid as a Rock !!!<BR>8. Do you get "looks" when driving your Fiero?<BR>Depends,on the way to work,at 4:30 A.M, NO, but on my way home...... <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/cool.gif"><BR>9. What sound system do you have in your Fiero?<BR>Stock.<BR>10. Do your relatives and friends like Fieros?<BR>My kid brother thinks it's cool.<BR>11.  Your Fiero?<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> I'm SOOOO glad it's mine!!!!!!<BR>12. Why do you think they cancelled the car (short answer please)?<BR>Very bad press due to flaws in the earlier models. Even though GM fixed the Bugs,Pontiac never could recover from lost sales........Barbecue, anyone?  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><BR>13. Do you want a new Fiero to be released?<BR>NO!<BR>14. If so, what would you want it to look like?<BR>What part of "NO" don't we understand?<BR>15. What plans do you have for your Fiero, in terms of upgrades, engine work, body kits, sound system, etc..<BR>1.Brakes and Suspension- crossed drilled rotors,front and rear swaybars with poly bushings,Koni struts,etc.<BR>2.Tranny-Find a Getrag and add Hi Perf clutch components<BR>3.Engine-Better Ign.coil,K&N filter,Hotter throttle body,Perf cam,...Dammit, the $%*& alarm clock woke me up again!<BR>16. Do you think Fiero's will rise in collectors value?<BR>Don't really know,and wouldn't care,I have the only car I've ever really wanted and will never part with it.<BR>17. If and when your Fiero finally does break down for good, will you keep it or junk it?</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE>With all the info and help on this site,I don't see how "breaking down for good" is even a remote possibility!||||reg||1
Z||000033||fierosound||05-11-2000||12:28 AM||||[QUOTE]Originally posted by Homicidal:<P>1. When did you start to like Fieros?<BR>- The BOND GT commercial<P>2. Why did you like them?<BR>- cool good looks, rustproof body<P>3. When and where did you first obtain your first Fiero?<BR>- consignment lot 1990 27,000km<P>4. What type of Fiero do you own?<BR>- 1987 Fiero GT V6 5-speed, burgundy/grey<P>5. What year and model do you like the best?<BR>- 1988 MERA or 88 GT T-top<P>6. Do you have a nice paint job on it?<BR>- still original, looks good<P>7. What does it run like?<BR>- still original, runs great<P>8. Do you get "looks" when driving your Fiero?<BR>- when is freshly waxed - ALWAYS<P>9. What sound system do you have in your Fiero?<BR>- killer custom  <A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/fierosound" TARGET=_blank>www.geocities.com/fierosound</A> <P>10. Do your relatives and friends like Fieros?<BR>- not especially<P>11.  Your Fiero?<BR>- they like mine, but not enough to buy one<P>12. Why do you think they cancelled the car (short answer please)?<BR>- lost sales to other 2-seaters<P>13. Do you want a new Fiero to be released?<BR>- don't really care<P>14. If so, what would you want it to look like?<P>15. What plans do you have for your Fiero, in terms of upgrades, engine work, body kits, sound system, etc..<BR>- 3.4L 220hp engine next project<P>16. Do you think Fiero's will rise in collectors value?<BR>- not for another 5-10 years, only concours condition models<P>17. If and when your Fiero finally does break down for good, will you keep it or junk it?<BR>- won't happen, unless it's totalled in accident<P><p>[This message has been edited by fierosound (edited 05-11-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000034||fieroshop||05-11-2000||01:43 AM||||  <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Homicidal:<BR><B>1. When did you start to like Fieros?<BR>When they first came out. I was a sales manager for Pontiac.<BR>2. Why did you like them?<BR>They were sporty looking and different.<BR>3. When and where did you first obtain your first Fiero?<BR>I finally bought my first Fiero in 1992<BR>4. What type of Fiero do you own?<BR>I own several but my favorite is an 88 GT<BR>5. What year and model do you like the best?<BR>88 GT<BR>6. Do you have a nice paint job on it?<BR>Yes and I am still repainting it primeraly for show.<BR>7. What does it run like?<BR>It is in great shape, considering I own a Fiero Shop.<BR>8. Do you get "looks" when driving your Fiero?<BR>Boy do I! I get asked what year is my car and who makes it. My 88 GT looks and drives like new. <BR>9. What sound system do you have in your Fiero?<BR>I have installed better speakers and a cd player from a 1992 Pontiac mini van, I also have the subwoofer system<BR>10. Do your relatives and friends like Fieros?<BR>Some do and some don't<BR>11.  Your Fiero?<BR>Yep<BR>12. Why do you think they cancelled the car (short answer please)?<BR>Ask Chevy<BR>13. Do you want a new Fiero to be released?<BR>Hard to say<BR>14. If so, what would you want it to look like?<BR>Don't know but it will have to be a sharp car.<BR>15. What plans do you have for your Fiero, in terms of upgrades, engine work, body kits, sound system, etc..<BR>Eventually I will upgrade the engine but for now I am doing a new paint, new rims and tires (17" wheels)<BR>16. Do you think Fiero's will rise in collectors value?<BR>Sure do<BR>17. If and when your Fiero finally does break down for good, will you keep it or junk it?</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Unless it gets in a wreck I will keep it and continue to repair it.<p>[This message has been edited by fieroshop (edited 05-11-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000035||Dan86gt3.8||05-11-2000||03:57 AM||||<BR>1. When did you start to like Fieros?<BR>The day my dad drug 2 of them up into I driveway, but more along the lines of when I saw one of the hotest chicks in my highschool drive a pearl white gt in the parking lot, she slowed down and said hi to me as I was mounting my 125 suzuki, I was 15 at the time<BR>2. Why did you like them?<BR>Loved the way the gt looked<BR>3. When and where did you first obtain your first Fiero?<BR>When I enherited my dads 86gt, guess it was about 2 years ago<BR>4. What type of Fiero do you own?<BR>86gt, black with silver ground effects, wit a serries 2 naturaly aspirated v6 done with an ace kit, 4 speed auto tranny<BR>5. What year and model do you like the best?<BR>I love any of the gt's 86-88 I guess, really like the t-top gt's also!<BR>6. Do you have a nice paint job on it?<BR>semi nice, good paint bad prep work (earl shieb's which was all I could afford at the time)<BR>7. What does it run like?<BR>runs damn great, has a tiny bit of an itle problem but soon to be fixed!<P>8. Do you get "looks" when driving your Fiero? yes but its usualy cause I make so much damn racket, I only run resonator tips (with a cat of course  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> ) I also play some loud music, old people love me they just cant get enough<P>9. What sound system do you have in your Fiero?a pioneer 35x4 watt tape deck, with a 6 disc changer mounted in a perfect location that was all original idea by me, umm pioneer 4x10s 2 ways in the dash, and some pioneer 2 way 6.5's custom mounted in the door, then 2 pioneer 8's in square "custom" boxes behind the seats, they are pushe by a rockford 175 watt amp (the ones before the punch series) I did all the wiring and box building myself, I also plan to get tweeters and reinstall my subs the fiero sound way <P>10. Do your relatives and friends like Fieros?<BR>most do, tall people like to *****  about no leg room but after I put the subs away no compliants there<BR>11.  Your Fiero?<BR>Ya my friends love it when I smoke ricers, they are usually scared shitless to when I pull my high speed cornering moves<BR>12. Why do you think they cancelled the car (short answer please)?<BR>it all boild down to is gm was some greedy greedy bastards, and they werent making the ultimate profit so the scrapped it because it didn't earn them enough<BR>13. Do you want a new Fiero to be released?<BR>hell yes!  same design throw in a couple new styling cues, the 88 suspension, offer a4 banger coupe, a 3800 coupe, then a gt fastback that would sport, you guessed it a 3.8 supercharged!  also you could make the fiero gt-x which would sport ethier the ls1 or the northstar, (we'll just leave that up to the engineers) also both 5 and 6 speed manuals will be offered, duh<BR>14. If so, what would you want it to look like?<BR>damn I alread answered that above oops, umm basically the same maybe change the lines up some but stil mid engine beast, offered in coupe and fastback, options like spoilers, ram air, and foglights are a must<BR>15. What plans do you have for your Fiero, in terms of upgrades, engine work, body kits, sound system, etc..<BR>want to keep this gt fix all the body panels ad ram air side scoops, my raised wing and lay ethier a bright yellow or navy blue metalic, maybe chop the roof a inch or two and add a over the roof snorkel intake.  after that I would yank my 3.8 out and bullet proof the bottom end then have the heads worked to thier fullest potential, and a custom cam and add ehtier a supercharger or a big fat turbo.  All this stuff would be matched up and built by a seroius engine builder.  Then I would have a getrag fully rebuilt with good stuff and have 3.73's or 4.10's put in.  Or just use the 6 speed with sequential gear select (that is if it really exists).  after thats taken care of some monster 12-13 inch crosdrilled slotted rotor, 4 piston caliper abs brakes would be added.  the suspension would be the coiover stuff from irm or whoever makes it, I would also track down thoose guys that put the mustang 2 front ends on fieros and have that done, I would top that off with some 17 inch wheels sporting z rated sticky sticky sticly tires!  Of course poly bushings and swaybars and the like throught, all the controll arms will be tubular, etc, etc, etc. as for the interior custom racing seats wth harnesses, gauges for everything from tack to boost gauge to baremetric pressure in russia.<P>After that I will go find some loley coupe that has ben abandoned, I will put a ferrari tesarosa kit on it and have the boys at design one do a tt north star on it.!<BR>ohh yes did I meantion I would need to win that 360 million dollar lotery, wait theres 2 winners o well!<BR>16. Do you think Fiero's will rise in collectors value?<BR>I dono I hope not that means they will be cheaper for me to buy!<BR>17. If and when your Fiero finally does break down for good, will you keep it or junk it?<BR>well my fiero is gona live forever, it's gona learn to fly......<P>||||reg||1
Z||000036||bHooper||05-11-2000||07:22 AM||||1. When did you start to like Fieros?<BR><B>1984</B><BR>2. Why did you like them?<BR><B>they were mid engine, and different</B><BR>3. When and where did you first obtain your first Fiero?<BR><B>Nov 3, 1989 in Winston Salem NC (35 miles away)</B><BR>4. What type of Fiero do you own?<BR><B>I still own that car, it is a 86.5 GT</B><BR>5. What year and model do you like the best?<BR><B>84 Indy, 86.5 GT, 88 Formula, 88 GT and I have seen one or SE that I like</B><BR>6. Do you have a nice paint job on it?<BR><B>If you consider orange peel, fade and the color of black enduraflex, nice</B><BR>7. What does it run like?<BR><B>dont know, just cranked it, for the 1st time in 4 years, the other night b4 spraying fuel in the manifold  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/eek.gif">... it was a little rough!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"></B><BR>8. Do you get "looks" when driving your Fiero?<BR><B>Yep, people walk by my house all the time and give me looks for working on this funny car with the engine in the back, and the body in the air</B><BR>9. What sound system do you have in your Fiero?<BR><B>a black hole in the console and 2 empty spaces in the dash... but somewhere I have a nice AIWA hu and soome components.</B><BR>10. Do your relatives and friends like Fieros?<BR><B>One friend does, of course he has a GT just like mine!  Everyone else thinks I need to be committed to charter</B><BR>11. Your Fiero?<BR><B>Your doing WHAT to that!?</B><BR>12. Why do you think they cancelled the car (short answer please)?<BR><B>Production numbers, bean counters, the threat on the corvette, and a tarnished image brought on my the earlier cars</B><BR>13. Do you want a new Fiero to be released?<BR><B>This is irelative... there WILL NEVER BE ANOTHER FIERO!  Someone else may eventually come out with a mid engine car, but not pontiac</B><BR>14. If so, what would you want it to look like?<BR><B>the Mach 5</B><BR>15. What plans do you have for your Fiero, in terms of upgrades, engine work, body kits, sound system, etc..<BR><B>I am have just put a new tranny on the car and plan to drive it for the 1st time in 4 years, next week.  Beyond that, possible 3.4 l conversion, leather interior and new suspension geometry</B><BR>16. Do you think Fiero's will rise in collectors value?<BR><B>some will, most want... 84 indys, 88 gt and formula</B><BR>17. If and when your Fiero finally does break down for good, will you keep it or junk it?<BR><B>that has happened, and haveing finally had time and a place, I am rebuilding it!</B>||||reg||1
Z||000037||Jay||05-11-2000||09:02 AM||||ALL THE WAY DOWN AT THE BOTTOM OF THIS PAGE NOBODY IS GONNA READ MY REPLY!!!<BR>MY FIRST CAR WAS A LADA, IT BROKE DOWN WAY OUTSIDE OF TORONTO IN A LITTLE TOWN.  RIGHT ACROSS THE STREET  WAS A DEALERSHIP WHICH HAD A 1984 FIERO SE.  I BOUGHT IT ON THE SPOT AND DROVE IT HOME.  I LOVED IT BUT HEAD GASKET WENT SO AFTER I REPAIRED IT I SOLD IT.  TEN YEARS WOULD PASS BEFORE I FOUND THE FIERO I ALWAYS WANTED...A GT.  <P>  I FOUND MY 86 GT IN A BAD PART OF TOWN.  IT BELONGED TO A DRUG DEALER WHO I BELIEVE WAS HIGH THE DAY I LEFT MY NUMBER ON HIS WINDSCREEN, ASKING IF HE WANTED TO SELL.  THAT NIGHT I GOT A CALL FROM HIM AND I WENT DOWN TO SEE THE CAR UP CLOSE.  IT WAS DISCUSTINGLY DIRTY, I MEAN YOU COULDN'T SIT IN IT FOR FEAR OF PLAGUE ENTERING YOUR CLOTHES.  THE FRONT HOOD WOULDN'T CLOSE PROPERLY AND THE EXHAUST WAS JUST HANGING THERE.  TO BE HONEST, I DIDN'T WANT THAT CAR!  BUT THE PRICE WAS RIGHT...$500 CANADIAN!!<P>I TOOK IT AND OVER THE WINTER RIPPED OUT THE INTERIOR AND PUT IN CUSTOM SEATS, HEADLINER, DOOR SKINS, CARPET AND PAINTED THE DASH ALL IN BLACK.  NEW RIMS AND RUBBER, FIXED EXHAUST, DID A TUNE UP AND SHE RAN BEAUTIFULLY.  I EVEN TOOK FIRST PLACE AT THE TORONTO FIERO SHOW FOR MY CLASS!!<P>  LAST YEAR THE ENGINE WENT.  I WAS ABOUT TO PUT IN A 3.8 SUPERCHARGED FROM A BONNEVILLE, BUT THEN I MET AND SAW JOHN NORMANS NORTHSTAR IN PERSON.  I WAS SOLD.  NORTHSTAR IT WOULD BE!  AFTER MONTHS OF SEARCHING FOR AN ENGINE I FINALLY FOUND ONE AT A TRANNY SHOP.  IT WAS A 97 STS NORTHSTAR WITH TRANNY FOR $1700 CANADIAN.  I HAD TO TAKE IT!  IT'S NOW GOING IN, HOPEFULLY TO BE READY BY JUNE.<P>  I JUST LOVE HOW THE GT'S LOOK, AND NOW WITH THIS CONVERSION, IT WILL GO LIKE IT SHOULD!!1||||reg||1
Z||000038||Monkeyman||05-11-2000||09:50 AM||||  <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Homicidal:<BR><B>1. When did you start to like Fieros?<BR>     From the beginning.  Detroit Auto Show.  '82 or '83.<P>2. Why did you like them?<BR>     Sporty, etc.<P>3. When and where did you first obtain your first Fiero?<BR>     Just last fall.  My wife bought it for me in Ohio.  ('86 2m4)<P>4. What type of Fiero do you own?<BR>     '86 2m4 (the Monkeymobile-parts car) and an '85 GT (the Grape Ape)<P>5. What year and model do you like the best?<BR>     Notchback GT  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>6. Do you have a nice paint job on it?<BR>     Mostly purple pearlized paint.  Needs repainted, though.  One of many "soon" projects.<P>7. What does it run like?<BR>     I'll tell you in a couple of days when I get it out of the shop.<P>8. Do you get "looks" when driving your Fiero?<BR>     I got great looks back when I was driving my plain Jane '86.  I can't wait to see the looks I'm sure to get once I get the Grape Ape on the road!<P>9. What sound system do you have in your Fiero?<BR>     Nothing at present.  Cassette head unit, CD changer, 5 1/4" separates custom mounted in the dash, a couple of amps and a sub.  Most of that in the next few weeks.  The rest sometime this winter.<P>10. Do your relatives and friends like Fieros?<BR>     My kid thinks it's "killer".  My wife "claims" that she doesn't like it, but...<P>11.  Your Fiero?<BR>     Don't understand the question.<P>12. Why do you think they cancelled the car (short answer please)?<BR>     Beancounters and too much competition with the Vette.<P>13. Do you want a new Fiero to be released?<BR>     Absolutely NOT!  It would change everything.  I wouldn't mind another mid-engined, 2 seat sporty car from GM if it was done right, but I'd like my Fiero to have a history.<P>15. What plans do you have for your Fiero, in terms of upgrades, engine work, body kits, sound system, etc..<BR>     5" wing stands, tinted windows, power ant, GA brakes, standard bushing upgrades, lowered, 3800SC, etc.<P>16. Do you think Fiero's will rise in collectors value?<BR>     Nope.  Not a chance.  Good for us, bad for collectors.<P>17. If and when your Fiero finally does break down for good, will you keep it or junk it?<BR>     No way, Jose!  Already been down that road.  I still have it sitting in my driveway.  If I get too many Fieros that have broken down, I'll just go the way that Doug Kinney and Fierodave have gone.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P><p>[This message has been edited by Monkeyman (edited 05-11-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000039||N_Man||05-11-2000||12:02 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Homicidal:<BR><B>1. When did you start to like Fieros?<BR>-About 3 years ago, when I spotted a GT that caught my intrest<P>2. Why did you like them?<BR>-origionally style, It looked so damn good.  Now its alot of things looks, handling, having a car thats a little bit different.<P>3. When and where did you first obtain your first Fiero?<BR>-About two months ago.<P>4. What type of Fiero do you own?<BR>-A beautiful blue 87GT<P>5. What year and model do you like the best?<BR>-I like the V6 5spd.  GT's are nice too(any year)<P>6. Do you have a nice paint job on it?<BR>-almost perfect!.  The grey ground effects have been painted to match the car courtisy of the previous owner.<P>7. What does it run like?<BR>-Runs like an engine with bad compression that burns almost as much oill as gas(but not for long)<P>8. Do you get "looks" when driving your Fiero?<BR>-all the time. Part of the reason I like it.<P>9. What sound system do you have in your Fiero?<BR>-Alpine head unit and 6 disk changer. JL 10"sub behind passenger seat(soon to come out though.)<P>10. Do your relatives and friends like Fieros?<BR>-some do some dont. but more do now that ive been laying down the persuasion.<P>11.  Your Fiero?<BR>-I cant get enough of it even with a poor engine.  With a new engine im sure a few more miles will end up on it.<P>12. Why do you think they cancelled the car (short answer please)?<BR>-GM doesn't know what there doing.  Cancelation of the F-bodies in a few years, bloody briliant.<P>13. Do you want a new Fiero to be released?<BR>-If its done right of course.<P>14. If so, what would you want it to look like?<BR>-The same but different.<P>15. What plans do you have for your Fiero, in terms of upgrades, engine work, body kits, sound system, etc..<BR>-New engine 3.4 if things go well.<BR>stock appearence.<BR>GM CD player, removal of the aftermarker stuff,  It came with the car and i could use the money if isold it.<P>16. Do you think Fiero's will rise in collectors value?<BR>-Yes<P>17. If and when your Fiero finally does break down for good, will you keep it or junk it?<BR>-Im not gonna let it break down for good <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><BR></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>||||reg||1
Z||000040||Standard||05-12-2000||03:36 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Homicidal:<BR><B>1. When did you start to like Fieros?</B> 3 years ago, saw one when I was looking for my first car.. ended up getting one!<P><B>2. Why did you like them?</B>  Unique!!  great handeling, awesome styling<P><B>3. When and where did you first obtain your first Fiero?</B> about 3 years ago at a used car lot<P><B>4. What type of Fiero do you own?</B> Black 1986 Fiero GT 5 speed, ac,cc,pw,pl,pm,rear defrost<P><B>5. What year and model do you like the best?</B>  Any year GT!<P><B>6. Do you have a nice paint job on it?</B>  not yet!<P><B>7. What does it run like?</B> loud!<P><B>8. Do you get "looks" when driving your Fiero?</B> all the time!<P><B>9. What sound system do you have in your Fiero?</B>  2 way pioneer 4x10's and 4x6's, pioneer deck and 10" sub soon<P><B>10. Do your relatives and friends like Fieros?</B>  yep<P><B>11.  Your Fiero?</B>  of course<P><B>12. Why do you think they cancelled the car (short answer please)?</B>  corperate politics, it was gonna kill the vette.. hehehe<P><B>13. Do you want a new Fiero to be released?</B>  not really<P><B>14. If so, what would you want it to look like?</B><P><B>15. What plans do you have for your Fiero, in terms of upgrades, engine work, body kits, sound system, etc..</B>  rebuild, maybe 3.4 swap, then turbo or nitrous.. side scoops <P><B>16. Do you think Fiero's will rise in collectors value?</B> i sure hope so!<P><B>17. If and when your Fiero finally does break down for good, will you keep it or junk it?</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE>  keep it forever!  as long as I have it, it'll run!<P>||||reg||1
Z||000041||2M4 Dale||05-12-2000||12:29 PM||||1. Since they started making them<BR>2. Sporty new Pontiac<BR>3. Private owner add in newspaper - just a little over a year ago.<BR>4. 87 Coupe<BR>5. 88 Formula<BR>6. Yes, fresh BLACK PPG Prismatique<BR>7. Runs about as good as a iron duck can<BR>8. Yes<BR>9. Jenson head unit and CD changer with Kenwood excellon 4X6 and Kenwood 4X10 coaxials. Also a 35w per Pheonix Saphire Gold amp pushing a Power Accoustic 8" sub in a RS Motorsports center console box...Sounds Great !!!<BR>10. Thats a toss up...some do - some don't<BR>11. Generally Yes<BR>12. To much competition for that other plastic "Chevy"<BR>13. NO<BR>14. -<BR>15. swap out the four clyinder...Maybe just a stock V6 would work.<BR>16. Yes, but it may take a while<BR>17. It won't break down for good...I'll just keep fixing it !!! ||||reg||6
Z||000042||Child Of Rod||05-12-2000||09:56 PM||||1. When did you start to like Fieros?<BR>7 years ago.  I read kitcar alot.<BR>2. Why did you like them?<BR>They were little and unique.  I feel that they look great just stock.<BR>3. When and where did you first obtain your first Fiero?<BR>A few weeks ago from some old lady.<BR>then my second the day after from a tow truck driver(no title, parts car).<BR>4. What type of Fiero do you own?<BR>1984 2m4<BR>1985 2m4(parts car)<P>5. What year and model do you like the best?<BR>1988 yellow formula..silver any year is a good follow up.<BR>6. Do you have a nice paint job on it?<BR>nope, I am just starting to work on mechanical stuff first, then I will get a nice paint job.<P>7. What does it run like?<BR>Rough,  at least till I swap the engines(3800SC, or 400cid SBC)<BR>8. Do you get "looks" when driving your Fiero?<BR>I can't drive them yet <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/redface.gif">)<BR>9. What sound system do you have in your Fiero?<BR>Stock.<BR>10. Do your relatives and friends like Fieros?<BR>Yes, they are very envious.  but I knowthey love my mustang.<BR>11.  Your Fiero?<BR>yep.<BR>12. Why do you think they cancelled the car (short answer please)?<BR>I dunno.<BR>13. Do you want a new Fiero to be released?<BR>YES,  but I would love them to release it in the old notchback style.  You know they still manufacture VW bugs in Mexico,  why not start up fieros?<BR>14. If so, what would you want it to look like?<BR>Old.<BR>15. What plans do you have for your Fiero, in terms of upgrades, engine work, body kits, sound system, etc..<P>V8 or 3800SC, new interior, new wheels.<P>16. Do you think Fiero's will rise in collectors value?<BR>Yes.<BR>17. If and when your Fiero finally does break down for good, will you keep it or junk it?[/B][/QUOTE]<BR>Keep it,  I'll be driving it when we all have electric vehicles<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000043||Coconut||11-19-2000||04:57 PM||||I really enjoyed this topic when I first became a member here <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>In light of all the new members that have joined us since then, I took the liberty of resurrecting this thread (I hope you don't mind, Homicidal)<P>Ok newbies or anyone else who hasn't responded to this post.....give us your thoughts please! (makes for even better reading than the National Enquirer) <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>Cruisin'<P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Coconut's_Signature_1.JPG"> ||||reg||1
Z||000044||Tryxalon||11-19-2000||05:39 PM||||1. When did you start to like Fieros? &lt;b&gt; 1984 &lt;/b&gt; <P>2. Why did you like them? &lt;b&gt; 2 seats+engine and little else in a low-slung sportscar with lots of leg room -- what's not to like?? &lt;/b&gt; <P>3. When and where did you first obtain your first Fiero? &lt;b&gt; In July 2000 as a "toy" or "project" &lt;/b&gt; <P>4. What type of Fiero do you own? &lt;b&gt; 85 SE 2m4 with a slowly dying 4cylinder &lt;/b&gt; <P>5. What year and model do you like the best?<BR>&lt;b&gt; Like the 84-85 notchback. Think the rounded nose, slantback look is too "cookie cutter". &lt;/b&gt;  <BR> <BR>6. Do you have a nice paint job on it? &lt;b&gt; No. Not yet. &lt;/b&gt; <P>7. What does it run like? &lt;b&gt;  Somewhat.  It is dying at 210,000 miles. &lt;/b&gt; <P>8. Do you get "looks" when driving your Fiero? &lt;b&gt; Yeah. But that is their problem. &lt;/b&gt; <P>9. What sound system do you have in your Fiero? &lt;b&gt; Stock. My hearing is bad enough from living through the 60's (rock & roll AND artillery!!!)that there is no need for any "wasted" money on stereo. &lt;/b&gt; <P>10. Do your relatives and friends like Fieros? &lt;b&gt; no. But again, that is their problem.&lt;/b&gt; <P>11. Your Fiero? &lt;b&gt; No, they don't like it either. &lt;/b&gt;  <P>12. Why do you think they cancelled the car (short answer please)? &lt;b&gt; Stupidity?? Rivalry?? Idiocy?? &lt;/b&gt; <P>13. Do you want a new Fiero to be released?<BR>&lt;b&gt; A new car with the same concept? Yes.  Restart production of the Fiero? ... maybe. Lot of updating to do .. wouldn't be the same. &lt;/b&gt; <P>14. If so, what would you want it to look like? &lt;b&gt; The Opel Speedster is a good place to start. &lt;/b&gt; <P>15. What plans do you have for your Fiero, in terms of upgrades, engine work, body kits, sound system, etc.. &lt;b&gt; Duct or vent the front "hood"  to allow better cooling and lower underbody air pressure, swap a 3100 auto v-6 I have in my garage into the engine bay, restore interior, paint eventually. &lt;/b&gt;  <P>16. Do you think Fiero's will rise in collectors value? &lt;b&gt; Eventually. &lt;/b&gt;   <P>17. If and when your Fiero finally does break down for good, will you keep it or junk it? &lt;b&gt; If I can fix it, it did not "break down for good". &lt;/b&gt; <BR><p>[This message has been edited by Tryxalon (edited 11-19-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000045||2xsess||11-19-2000||06:02 PM||||1. When did you start to like Fieros?<B>1990 when I was looking for my first car</B><P>2. Why did you like them?<B> I loved the low stance and the body design</B><P>3. When and where did you first obtain your first Fiero?<B>In 1993 I bought an 84 coupe from a guy near Allentown PA</B><P>4. What type of Fiero do you own?<B>1985 GT 4spd with an 86GT interior</B><P>5. What year and model do you like the best?<B> I can't pick just one, I like the 85GT and the 88GT t-top and of course the Indy</B><P>6. Do you have a nice paint job on it?<B>not yet  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"></B><P>7. What does it run like?<B>like a car with 100,000 miles on it,kind of rough right now but I'm working on it</B><P>8. Do you get "looks" when driving your Fiero?<B>Yep</B>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>9. What sound system do you have in your Fiero?<B> JVC Kameleon CD player and Kenwood 4x10s</B><P>10. Do your relatives and friends like Fieros? <B> My family likes them but still think I'm nuts</B><P>11.  Your Fiero?<B> but of course</B><P>12. Why do you think they cancelled the car (short answer please)?<B> Bad image brought on by early mechanical malfunctions</B><P>13. Do you want a new Fiero to be released?<B> No, I think it would be cool if GM introduced a midengine car under a different name though</B><P>14. If so, what would you want it to look like?<B> Kind of like the NSX...flame suit on</B><P>15. What plans do you have for your Fiero, in terms of upgrades, engine work, body kits, sound system, etc..<B> 3.2,new white pearl paint,refurbish interior, thinking about subs like Fierosound has and it will soon have white/blue face gauges.</B><P>16. Do you think Fiero's will rise in collectors value?<B> eventually</B><P>17. If and when your Fiero finally does break down for good, will you keep it or junk it?<B> break down for good? don't think that's possible. The only reason I'd get rid of it is if the frame rots out from under it</B>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>------------------<BR>Jeff<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/My_car_(large)sig_1.JPG">  <p>[This message has been edited by 2xsess (edited 11-20-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000046||AkursedX||11-19-2000||06:28 PM||||1. When did you start to like Fieros?  I liked them when I was little kid, but then I forgot about them, and I once again fell in love with them at the beginning of this year when I was looking for a cheap, and relativley high performance sports car with potential for lots of mods.<P>2. Why did you like them?  The best reason is probably because they are so unique.  And they are excellent handlers<P>3. When and where did you first obtain your first Fiero? April 2000, Downtown Buffalo NY<P>4. What type of Fiero do you own? 1988 Fiero GT.  Red, Gold rims, no spoiler, tan interior, power locks and windows, cruise, and premium sound.  (I think that's all the options)<P>5. What year and model do you like the best? 1987 Blue Formula with T-tops and black rims, *drool*<P>6. Do you have a nice paint job on it?  yeah, but it has a few chips on the front decklid<P>7. What does it run like?  Excellent, high oil pressure and compression, no oil leaks.<P>8. Do you get "looks" when driving your Fiero?  Sometimes, I get the occaisional "thumbs up" from people<P>9. What sound system do you have in your Fiero?  Kenwood KDC3011 head unit (will be replaced in the spring)  Blaupunkt overdrive 4x6's, and Infinity Kappa 4" components in the fronts.<P>10. Do your relatives and friends like Fieros?  Not really.  It's a "deathtrap"<P>11.  Your Fiero?  They all love mine though<P>12. Why do you think they cancelled the car (short answer please)?  Vette Competetion, the saturn project, bad publicity, take your pick.<P>13. Do you want a new Fiero to be released?  Not really<P>14. If so, what would you want it to look like?  <P>15. What plans do you have for your Fiero, in terms of upgrades, engine work, body kits, sound system, etc..  Well my suspension is all done (poly all around, KYB's and Eibachs)  I still want to buy 17 inch rims this winter.  Then next winter comes my engine project.  I'm gonna stick with the 2.8 or  3.1 and just see how much power I can get out of it, that my budget will allow me for though  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>16. Do you think Fiero's will rise in collectors value?  I think the low mileage rare colored and styled ones will while the rest will continue to depreciate<P>17. If and when your Fiero finally does break down for good, will you keep it or junk it?  Oh I'll definietly keep it.  <P>||||reg||7
Z||000047||Fformula88||11-19-2000||06:47 PM||||1. When did you start to like Fieros?<BR>A: When my dad bought his 87 coupe in May 1990 (I was 13)<P>2. Why did you like them?<BR>A: Thought it was an awesome sports car!<P>3. When and where did you first obtain your first Fiero?<BR>A:  My one and only was bought in June 1996 off a used car lot.<P>4. What type of Fiero do you own?<BR>A: 1988 Fiero Formula<P>5. What year and model do you like the best?<BR>A: Same as #4.  I also like the GT's and 84 Indy's.  Actaully, I like them all but am biased to my model!<P>6. Do you have a nice paint job on it?<BR>A:  The paint is in fabulous shape for a 13 year old car with 80,000 miles!  A few scratches, couple stone chips on front fascia but overall its VERY good!<P>7. What does it run like?<BR>A:  Runs good... have had a lot of problems with it at idle but its slowly getting better.  Needs a new cat.<P>8. Do you get "looks" when driving your Fiero?<BR>A:  I am amazed at how many looks I do get.  The one that blew me away was when a guy in a C4 Vette convertable parked next to me and was checkin out my car!<P>9. What sound system do you have in your Fiero?<BR>A: JBL 4x10's in front and an Alpine head unit.... no other mods yet.  I do want new 4x6's too.<P>10. Do your relatives and friends like Fieros?<BR>A:  No one is as crazy about them as me... but they all say nice things about it.<P>11. Your Fiero?<BR>A: See above<P>12. Why do you think they cancelled the car (short answer please)?<BR>A: GM politics<P>13. Do you want a new Fiero to be released?<BR>A:  If it followed the Fiero's design and layout... yes<P>14. If so, what would you want it to look like?<BR>A:  A design that borrows from the original Fiero's<P>15. What plans do you have for your Fiero, in terms of upgrades, engine work, body kits, sound system, etc..<BR>A:  New 4x6's for the sail panels, I'd also like to do a 3400 conversion.  Maybe in a couple years!<P>16. Do you think Fiero's will rise in collectors value?<BR>A:  I think they will have some collectors value, for certain models.  Especially the 88's.<P>17. If and when your Fiero finally does break down for good, will you keep it or junk it?<BR>A:  Break down for good?!?  Not going to happen... I'll keep it going! ||||reg||1
Z||000048||87GTZ34||11-19-2000||06:52 PM||||1. When did you start to like Fieros?<P>   Aug '98.<P>2. Why did you like them?<BR>   timeless looks and great potential to be an killer sports car.<P>3. When and where did you first obtain your first Fiero?<BR>   From a low budget usd car lot in Oct '98.<P>4. What type of Fiero do you own?<BR>   Maroon '87 GT loaded.<P>5. What year and model do you like the best?<BR>   '87 or '88 GT fastback.<P>6. Do you have a nice paint job on it?<BR>   Okay but I will have a custom paint job when complete.<P>7. What does it run like?<P>   Hasn't run since Nov '99 when the engine (that the butcher used car dealer put in it) started knocking after I put 450 mi on the car.<P>8. Do you get "looks" when driving your Fiero? <BR>Used to...<P>9. What sound system do you have in your Fiero? <BR>Took out non-working Sony, haven't decided what to put in yet.<P>10. Do your relatives and friends like Fieros? Not really.<P>11. Your Fiero? Not yet...<P>12. Why do you think they cancelled the car (short answer please)? couldn't improve it performance wise (to keep sales moving) as it encroached into the camaro/ta and vette space.<P>13. Do you want a new Fiero to be released?<BR>No.<P>14. If so, what would you want it to look like?<P>N/A<P>15. What plans do you have for your Fiero, in terms of upgrades, engine work, body kits, sound system, etc..<P>  Already purchased a '96 3.4 dohc. currently planning out eng & chassis upgrades.<P>16. Do you think Fiero's will rise in collectors value?<BR>  Yes.<P>17. If and when your Fiero finally does break down for good, will you keep it or junk it?<P>  I probably won't keep a broken car unless it is worth something and appreciating.<P>||||reg||1
Z||000049||alpha||11-19-2000||06:58 PM||||1. When did you start to like Fieros?<P>About 3 years ago.<P>2. Why did you like them?<P>I had just crashed my previous car and was looking for cheap transportation which was sporty and different from the rest of the croud.<P>3. When and where did you first obtain your first Fiero?<P>Haverhill, MA. Shortly after I began to really get interested in them.<P>4. What type of Fiero do you own?<P>86 GT<P>5. What year and model do you like the best?<P>Pretty much any fastback, but I love them all!<P>6. Do you have a nice paint job on it?<P>Basically, when I did the body swap I painted several of the body panels. Most of them came out good, but I am going to have to repaint the right door skin when I get the chance.<P>7. What does it run like?<P>Basically okay, the engine is begining to get a little tired.<P>8. Do you get "looks" when driving your Fiero?<P>Some. For awhile I was driving with a "52" on the side which got a lot of looks.<P>9. What sound system do you have in your Fiero?<P>Pioneer 45DH Head, Jenson 4X10 in the dash and Pioneers in the headrests.<P>10. Do your relatives and friends like Fieros?<P>My father just bought an 88 GT, and the rest of my family is pretty supportive.<P>11.  Your Fiero?<P>Yeah, I guess.<P>12. Why do you think they cancelled the car (short answer please)?<P>I am going to refrain from answering this because there are too many reasons and it would take forever.<P>13. Do you want a new Fiero to be released?<P>Not really, its not going to happen anyway.<P>14. If so, what would you want it to look like?<P>n/a<P>15. What plans do you have for your Fiero, in terms of upgrades, engine work, body kits, sound system, etc..<P>I'd like to do a 3800 swap next summer, I have to finish putting the rest of the poly on, I need to  buy some autocross tires for next year too.<P>16. Do you think Fiero's will rise in collectors value?<P>Eventually yes, there is no question.<P>17. If and when your Fiero finally does break down for good, will you keep it or junk it?<P>If it broke down no way. I would fix it, no matter what went wrong. If I crash it or something I would strip it and then use/sell the parts...then get another Fiero.<P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://fiero.dhs.org/fiero/sig.jpg">   <BR>   <A HREF="mailto:douglas_knight@umit.maine.edu">douglas_knight@umit.maine.edu</A> ||||reg||1
Z||000050||hugh||11-19-2000||06:59 PM||||#1 Early 2000<BR>#2 I don't want to have the same thing as everyone else<BR>#3 Shreveport La., May 2000<BR>#4 GT<BR>#5 88GT<BR>#6 original paint(red)<BR>#7 It runs ok<BR>#8 Definately<BR>#9 Stock(I think)<BR>#10 Not necessarily<BR>#11 Yes<BR>#12 With business,It is always the bottom line!<BR>#13 no<BR>#14 ------<BR>#15 I am going to replace the 750 holley with the John Lingenfelter superam settup,DFI,and upgrade exhaust.<BR>#16 Definately yes.<BR>#17 I'm 60,It will probably outlast me.<BR><P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/hugh_sig.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000051||JBGehling||11-19-2000||07:15 PM||||1. When did you start to like Fieros?<P>I started liking them in 1988 when my dad bought a red 88 GT (which was just recently given to me). My enthusiasm grew when my grandad bought an 88 Formula (because he liked my dad's so much  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">)<P>2. Why did you like them?<P>In my opinion, these are some of the greatest looking cars ever and you just get so much for your money!<P>3. When and where did you first obtain your first Fiero?<P>My dad just turned over his 88 GT to me a few months back when I got my license.<P>4. What type of Fiero do you own?<P>Red 88 GT<P>5. What year and model do you like the best?<P>88 GT  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> (though I do think the 85 GT's look really spiffy)<P>6. Do you have a nice paint job on it?<P>VERY nice paint job<P>7. What does it run like?<P>it runs great!<P>8. Do you get "looks" when driving your Fiero?<P>oh yeh, though my current girlfriend doesn't like it.<P>9. What sound system do you have in your Fiero?<P>stock<P>10. Do your relatives and friends like Fieros?<P>My grandad loves them<P>11. Your Fiero?<P>Red, 88 GT, all options (save leather and t-tops), auto, 62,000, rear wing, almost purely stock (though I plan to turbo-charge it)<P>12. Why do you think they cancelled the car (short answer please)?<P>it wasn't selling  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>13. Do you want a new Fiero to be released?<P>yeh, especially if they would just use that great looking 89 prototype!<P>14. If so, what would you want it to look like?<P>(see last answer)<P>15. What plans do you have for your Fiero, in terms of upgrades, engine work, body kits, sound system, etc..<P>I plan to turbocharge it, add leather interior, cd-player, buy another rear decklid (W/O the spoiler), maybe some new wheels...<P>16. Do you think Fiero's will rise in collectors value?<P>definitely! It's numbers are decreasing quite frequently (heck, a junkyard here in Lexington, SC, has 8 coupes!) not to mention that it's a really great car.<P>17. If and when your Fiero finally does break down for good, will you keep it or junk it?<P>hmmmm... probably keep, though it would depend how badly it broke down  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>||||reg||1
Z||000052||trigger||11-19-2000||07:43 PM||||1. When did you start to like Fieros?  When I saw an Indy when I was five, now I'm 15.5<P>2. Why did you like them?  Good gas mileage, handling, fun to drive, rice killer.<P>3. When and where did you first obtain your first Fiero?  March, 1999 1988 coupe. Used car dealership in Dubuque, Iowa which is 30 min. East of me for 1430.<P>4. What type of Fiero do you own?  1988 Coupe 4cyl. auto. Catch me if you can donut eater, red.<P>5. What year and model do you like the best?<BR>	88 Coupe, Indy, 85 GT, 86 SE, I guess the fastbacks are ok.<P>6. Do you have a nice paint job on it?  Ok<P>7. What does it run like?  I've put a reasonable amount of work for a 12 year old 115,000 mile car.  Just did a balljoint, think I need a 02 sensor, now.<P>8. Do you get "looks" when driving your Fiero?  Hell, yeah.  I do a lot of looking out of my rear view mirror too, he he he.<P>9. What sound system do you have in your Fiero?  Getting new speakers for Christmas, but now optimus detachable face tape deck, optimus rear speakers.<P>10. Do your relatives and friends like Fieros?  Dad, yes but he is tired of it breaking, but it has been good for the last little while.  Mom, yes but she thinks I take corners too fast.  Friends put up with me.  My friends that are twins, one wants a fiero the other wants a Ford Mustink.<P>11. Your Fiero?  They have to<P>12. Why do you think they cancelled the car (short answer please)?  1. Corvette people were mad cause their vettes couldn't keep up.  <BR>2. Can you say eeediots?  3. Look at the Aztec.<BR>                  <BR>13. Do you want a new Fiero to be released?<BR>no.<BR>                           <BR>14. If so, what would you want it to look like? no<P>15. What plans do you have for your Fiero, in terms of upgrades, engine work, body kits, sound system, etc.. installed power trunk, getting power windows, and rims, spoiler, sunroof paint.  This spring I am picking up a <BR>86 SE V6 5 sd.  Will get sunroof, spoiler, lowered, rims, rebuilt w/9.5:1 forged pistons, plus 2 cam(at least), roller rockers, custum geared tranny, hi po ingnition, all the good stuff.<BR>                           <BR>16. Do you think Fiero's will rise in collectors value?  Eventually.<P>17. If and when your Fiero finally does break down for good, will you keep it or junk it?  The if already happened.  Break for good, yeah right.  Too good a little car.  If I get lucky a S/C gen 2 3.8 might just happen to get dropped in the trunk.<P>------------------<BR>Honestly officer, I was just keeping up with the flow of traffic.  I know there aren't any cars in the area, that's how far behind I am.||||reg||1
Z||000053||fieroparts.com||11-19-2000||07:49 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Homicidal:<BR><B>1. When did you start to like Fieros?<BR> 1989<P>2. Why did you like them? cute<P>3. When and where did you first obtain your first Fiero? mass. 1990<P>4. What type of Fiero do you own? <BR>1988 gt  org. t-toper 117 miles<BR>1988 coupe<BR>1986 coupe  30,000 miles<P>5. What year and model do you like the best?<BR>1988 gt<P>6. Do you have a nice paint job on it?<BR>yes<P>7. What does it run like?<BR>bat out of hell<P>8. Do you get "looks" when driving your Fiero?<BR>the 88 coupe   O YA<P>9. What sound system do you have in your Fiero?<BR>stock<P>10. Do your relatives and friends like Fieros? some<BR>11.  Your Fiero?<P>12. Why do you think they cancelled the car (short answer please)?<P><BR>13. Do you want a new Fiero to be released?<BR>no<P>14. If so, what would you want it to look like?<P>15. What plans do you have for your Fiero, in terms of upgrades, engine work, body kits, sound system, etc..<P>16. Do you think Fiero's will rise in collectors value?<BR>yes they will<P>17. If and when your Fiero finally does break down for good, will you keep it or junk it?</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>||||reg||1
Z||000054||gkozlov||11-19-2000||08:39 PM||||1. When did you start to like Fieros?<BR>Twelve years ago when I saw and bought my 84.<BR>2. Why did you like them?<BR>Cheap and Fun<BR>3. When and where did you first obtain your first Fiero?<BR>My fathers friend owned a used car lot.<BR>4. What type of Fiero do you own?<BR>86 SE<BR>5. What year and model do you like the best?<BR>87 SE<BR>6. Do you have a nice paint job on it?<BR>NO<BR>7. What does it run like?<BR>Its not the fastest car Ive ever driven. But, cant beat it for the buck.<BR>8. Do you get "looks" when driving your Fiero?<BR>Oh yeah. Ive got an really outrageous whales tale spoiler and racing stripes<BR>9. What sound system do you have in your Fiero?<BR>Alpine CD player, Alpine 75X4 and Rockford Fosgate Punch 40 Amps, Pioneer 6X9's up front and 4X6's in sails and A kicker Substation 8" sub.<BR>10. Do your relatives and friends like Fieros?<BR>Some do and some dont.<BR>11. Your Fiero?<BR>Some do and some dont.<BR>12. Why do you think they cancelled the car (short answer please)?<BR>Bad reputation from 84's<BR>13. Do you want a new Fiero to be released?<BR>Id love it.<BR>14. If so, what would you want it to look like?<BR>Id like it to at least resemble ours.<BR>15. What plans do you have for your Fiero, in terms of upgrades, engine work, body kits, sound system, etc..<BR>Id like to paint it.<BR>16. Do you think Fiero's will rise in collectors value?<BR>No not really.<BR>17. If and when your Fiero finally does break down for good, will you keep it or junk it?<BR>Mine is really not worth keeping. Its kinda rouph.<BR><P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sign1_3.jpg">  <BR><A HREF="http://g.kozlov.tripod.com/gkozlov.htm" TARGET=_blank>GKozlovs Fiero Site</A>||||reg||1
Z||000055||sqoach||11-19-2000||08:45 PM||||1. When did you start to like Fieros?<BR>   i just saw a pic of one and i thought it was cool<BR>2. Why did you like them?<BR>   i like little cars and sports cars<BR>3. When and where did you first obtain your first Fiero?<BR>   march 2000 in okc, oklahoma<BR>4. What type of Fiero do you own?<BR>   1986 sport coupe<BR>5. What year and model do you like the best?<BR>   i don't know yet, i've only had one<BR>6. Do you have a nice paint job on it?<BR>   nope...faded emerald green...i think it use to be nice...lol<BR>7. What does it run like?<BR>   sadly, it's not running too good right now<BR>8. Do you get "looks" when driving your Fiero?<BR>   yes...because i'm one of the only ones in town with one ( also my hotwheels licence plate  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> )<BR>9. What sound system do you have in your Fiero?<BR>   replaced the stock speakers and added a cd player<BR>10. Do your relatives and friends like Fieros?<BR>    uh....maybe.  if they don't then they're losers!<BR>11. Your Fiero?<BR>    evry1 tells me they like it, so i guess<BR>12. Why do you think they cancelled the car (short answer please)?<BR>    i think it was from the earlier models having engine fires...they got a bad rap after that<BR>13. Do you want a new Fiero to be released?<BR>    no, cuz i wouldn't be able to afford it<BR>14. If so, what would you want it to look like?<BR>    i'd just want it to be cheap<BR>15. What plans do you have for your Fiero, in terms of upgrades, engine work, body kits, sound system, etc..<BR>    well, when i get my new SE, new front end, side scoops, hood scoop, trunk scoop maybe, custom spoiler, 16s, good system, custom paint (man that's gonna cost a lot)<BR>16. Do you think Fiero's will rise in collectors value?<BR>    if no1 makes the fiero again<BR>17. If and when your Fiero finally does break down for good, will you keep it or junk it?<BR>    hmm...i'm not sure about that, but i guess i'll find out soon enough<P><P>------------------<BR>sQoaCh||||reg||6
Z||000056||Terrible Tom||11-19-2000||08:45 PM||||[QUOTE]Originally posted by Homicidal:<BR>[B]1. When did you start to like Fieros?<P>To start, when the Fiero came out in '84 I hated them!  As a former Vette owner ('74 L-82) I saw the Fiero as a cheap try to copy the almighty Vette.  Anyway, the Vette was sold in 1980 for the downpayment on our first house.<P>In 1989 our youngest son (of 4) got his license and a car and my wife announced she wanted a two seater car so she would never have to cart kids around again!  She decided on one of those "cute" Fiero fastbacks, which, by the way Pontiac had just announced they were discontinuing, so we trotted off to the dealership to get one for a good deal.  Well, that wasn't the case as the dealer was adding a $1,000 premium to the $15,000 sticker price as these would be "classics".  Needless to say, they weren't impressed with my $9,000 offer.  However, they did have a perfect 86 SE 2.8 on the lot with 18,000 miles and I was able to buy it for $5,000!  My wife was disappointed it wasn't a fastback but I told her you can't tell the difference from the inside.<P>To make a long story longer, I drove the Fiero home from the dealership and fell in love with it!  It was quick and handled well.  Sort of reminded me of being in the old Vette sitting close to the ground in the Fiero.  The love affair with the Fiero has never ended.  It's sitting outside with 122,000 miles and two cross country trips under it's belt.  Still is just as much fun to drive as the first day I bought it.  <BR>     <P>2. Why did you like them? - See above.<P>3. When and where did you first obtain your first Fiero? - See above.<P>4. What type of Fiero do you own? Silver 86 SE V6 -4 speed. <P>5. What year and model do you like the best?  All V6 models (sorry Duke guys).<P>6. Do you have a nice paint job on it?  No, The car was repainted a number of years ago after an accident and it has not held up well.  I'm planning a total restoration and repowering next year.<P>7. What does it run like?  Still runs strong.  Doesn't burn oil and stills scats when I get on it.<P>8. Do you get "looks" when driving your Fiero? Not with the faded paint job!<P>9. What sound system do you have in your Fiero? Stock (speakers need to be replaced).<P>10. Do your relatives and friends like Fieros?<BR>My wife was driving it in the accident a few years ago.  She T-boned a guy who pulled out in front of her.  I had to beg the insurance company not to total it.  Since the accident, she doesn't like it as she thinks she could have stopped in time if the car had power brakes.  She is now into her SUV and I have the Fiero.<P>11.  Your Fiero? See above.<P>12. Why do you think they cancelled the car (short answer please)?  Because of the bad reputation (fires).  GM has been parinoid since Nader got them with the Corvair.  Also, GM probably figured they would have to make major investments in the car due to the intro of the MR2.  two strikes and you're out in GM land!<P>13. Do you want a new Fiero to be released?  No!!!  I love the old ones too much.  Wouldn't want to have to make comparisons (remember the Vette story above).<P>14. If so, what would you want it to look like?<P>15. What plans do you have for your Fiero, in terms of upgrades, engine work, body kits, sound system, etc.. Good question, restoration planned for next year.  new powerplant (maybe a V8 Archie!), suspension overhaul (ball joints, poly, struts) paint (silver) leather seats etc.<P>16. Do you think Fiero's will rise in collectors value? Don't care as I'll never sell mine. (Hope they go down in value so I can buy a cheap parts car)<P>17. If and when your Fiero finally does break down for good, will you keep it or junk it?  Any breakdown can be repaired.  I fear losing it in an accident.  If so, I'll find another one!  That's what love is all about!<P>||||reg||1
Z||000057||Terrible Tom||11-19-2000||08:45 PM||||Sorry for the double post.<p>[This message has been edited by Terrible Tom (edited 11-19-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000058||StuGood||11-19-2000||11:44 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Homicidal:<BR><B>1. When did you start to like Fieros?</B><BR>Love at first sight - probably 1984. <BR><B>2. Why did you like them?</B><BR>Looks cool; plastic, midengine two-seater; it's the kit car I always wanted, minus the 5 years of hard work! <BR><B>3. When and where did you first obtain your first Fiero?</B>May, 1986; Scholfield Pontiac, Wichita KS.<BR><B>4. What type of Fiero do you own?</B><BR>1988 Coupe; 1987 GT; 1986 SE 4-speed V6; 1986 SE Auto V6.<BR><B>5. What year and model do you like the best?</B>1988 GT<BR><B>6. Do you have a nice paint job on it?</B><BR>All have the original paint - Only the 1986 SE 4-speed V6 is still what I'd call "nice." <BR><B>7. What does it run like?</B>All are starting to show their age, at this point.  Got some work ahead of me!<BR><B>8. Do you get "looks" when driving your Fiero?</B>Fairly often - not as much as in 1986, though!<BR><B>9. What sound system do you have in your Fiero?</B>Stock - all have the Delco AM/FM casette units. <BR><B>10. Do your relatives and friends like Fieros?</B>Not all - quite a few do.  But, face it, they're not for everybody.<BR><B>11. Your Fiero?</B>Yes- after they go for a ride in it! <BR><B>12. Why do you think they cancelled the car (short answer please)?</B>Corvette threat; bad rep.<BR><B>13. Do you want a new Fiero to be released?</B>Yes- but only if they do a good job of it.  And make lots of parts useable for the "old" Fieros - to replenish our salvage yards, y'know  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">!<BR><B>14. If so, what would you want it to look like?</B>Very similar to the "old" Fiero - and make the mounting points identical! <BR><B>15. What plans do you have for your Fiero, in terms of upgrades, engine work, body kits, sound system, etc..</B>Currently investigating engine swaps.  Better headlight actuators, and "Winky" lights all around!    <BR><B>16. Do you think Fiero's will rise in collectors value?</B> Possible - but I'm not betting my future on it!  Let's say "slightly."  Probably on the upturn fairly soon, but not a steep slope.<BR><B>17. If and when your Fiero finally does break down for good, will you keep it or junk it?</B>I'll keep it, at least as a parts car.<HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>||||reg||6
Z||000059||Gwynn||11-20-2000||12:17 AM||||1. When did you start to like Fieros? 10 years ago<P>2. Why did you like them? Great for picking up girls<P>3. When and where did you first obtain your first Fiero? Calgary, 10 years ago<P>4. What type of Fiero do you own? 86 2m4 Black<P>5. What year and model do you like the best? 88 GT.<P>6. Do you have a nice paint job on it? Yes<P>7. What does it run like? Great<P>8. Do you get "looks" when driving your Fiero? Not really<P>9. What sound system do you have in your Fiero? Pioneer tape with 12 pack CD, 10" sub with home built box, Alpine 500 Watt amp.<P>10. Do your relatives and friends like Fieros? Some<P>11. Your Fiero? Loves me.<P>12. Why do you think they canceled the car (short answer please)? The Fiero had unlimited growth potential while the Camero/TA line wasn't <BR>taking off. GM pulled the Fiero for the more expensive lines.<P>13. Do you want a new Fiero to be released? Yes, I would buy one brand new.<P>14. If so, what would you want it to look like? How about starting where they left off.<P>15. What plans do you have for your Fiero, in terms of upgrades, engine work, body kits, sound system, etc.. Lots<P>16. Do you think Fiero's will rise in collectors value? Absolutely.<P>17. If and when your Fiero finally does break down for good, will you keep it or junk it? I won't be letting it break down.<P><BR>||||reg||14
Z||000060||Cheever2||11-20-2000||01:04 AM||||<B>Long question... so why do you want to know?<BR>Guess this will prove what I been saying about how I could talk about Fieros all night.</B><BR>1. When did you start to like Fieros?<B>When I first got a good look at the interior of one & loved it.</B><BR>2. Why did you like them?<B>Two-seater, small.</B><BR>3. When and where did you first obtain your first Fiero?<B>When my daily driver Grand Am died; I had been reading Kit Car Magazine and was impressed with things people do with Fieros.  Bought first one 14 months ago.</B><BR>4. What type of Fiero do you own?<B>(A)-88 GT; (B)-88 Coupe</B><BR>5. What year and model do you like the best?<B>All of them.  Maybe 88 GT's best.</B><BR>6. Do you have a nice paint job on it?<B>Just have the original paint, which is still nice.</B><BR>7. What does it run like?<B>(A)-GT: stock V6 runs great! (B)-4 cyl: runs like a 4 cyl.</B><BR>8. Do you get "looks" when driving your Fiero?<B>Yes, often.  At first didn't know if I was going to like that cause I'm not a show-off, but I DO like it.</B><BR>9. What sound system do you have in your Fiero?<B>Stock radio/cassette, nothing special.  The coupe has only 1 speaker working.</B><BR>10. Do your relatives and friends like Fieros?<B>Not especially, but they haven't driven one yet.</B><BR>11. Your Fiero?<B>You mean do they like MY Fiero?  I think so but they're not saying much; they aren't "car people"  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"> </B><BR>12. Why do you think they cancelled the car (short answer please)?<B>I thought it was due to unsatisfactory sales numbers.</B><BR>13. Do you want a new Fiero to be released?<BR><B>No.  It just wouldn't be right, and wouldn't be the same.  Any new version would cost way too much and wouldn't be anything like the original.</B><BR>14. If so, what would you want it to look like?<B>n/a</B><BR>15. What plans do you have for your Fiero, in terms of upgrades, engine work, body kits, sound system, etc.<B>(A)-GT: Fino kit, but I'm dreaming; (B)-Coupe: I like it stock, just want to fix things & make it nice, but maybe big engine someday, and leather seats would be nice.</B><BR>16. Do you think Fiero's will rise in collectors value?<B>No I don't, sadly. Not enough interest to keep the Excitement alive.</B><BR>17. If and when your Fiero finally does break down for good, will you keep it or junk it?<B>I've already had my wrecked GT sitting in the garage collecting dust for a year now.</B><P><B>Did I win?  What do I get?</B><BR>||||reg||1
Z||000061||Songman||11-20-2000||01:57 AM||||1. When did you start to like Fieros? <B>Saw a Fiero in a magazine ad when I was a senior in high school in 1982. They were just about to come out and I loved them!</B><P>2. Why did you like them? <B>I had a Fiat X1/9 and the Fiero body design was pretty much a takeoff from it.</B><P>3. When and where did you first obtain your first Fiero? <B>About 7-8 years ago I put a set of aftermarket wheels on my Jag XJS and traded the stockers to a buddy of mine for a white 84 coupe.</B><P>4. What type of Fiero do you own? <B>Red 88 Formula, white 88 coupe, burgundy 87 GT, white 84 coupe </B><P>5. What year and model do you like the best? <B>I like the 88 GTs and Formulas</B><P>6. Do you have a nice paint job on it? <B>The white 88 is nice, the others need redone.</B><P>7. What does it run like? <B>Both 88s run great! The 87 and 84 have been sitting.</B><P>8. Do you get "looks" when driving your Fiero? <B>I get looks getting in and out of them for sure! I'm 6'2" and people wonder how I fold into it!</B><P>9. What sound system do you have in your Fiero? <B>Sony CD in 88 coupe. All stock other than that.</B><P>10. Do your relatives and friends like Fieros? <B>They are not really into them.</B><P>11. Your Fiero? <B>Same as above.</B><P>12. Why do you think they cancelled the car (short answer please)? <B>Bad press.</B><P>13. Do you want a new Fiero to be released? <B>Doesn't really matter to me. Hope they don't hang a GTO badge on some front wheel drive toy though.</B><P>14. If so, what would you want it to look like?<P>15. What plans do you have for your Fiero, in terms of upgrades, engine work, body kits, sound system, etc.. <B>Eventually build a body kit on the 84. Leave the 88s stock. May sell the 88 coupe later.</B><P>16. Do you think Fiero's will rise in collectors value? <B>In some circles. Overall, I doubt that they will ever be very expensive.</B><P>17. If and when your Fiero finally does break down for good, will you keep it or junk it? <B>I buy all my cars with plans to keep them usually. Eventually, they get sold or traded. I don't junk anything. Everything has a use one way or another.</B>||||reg||6
Z||000062||RNGCRSH||11-20-2000||03:09 AM||||1. When did you start to like Fieros?<BR>1983, the first one I laid eyes on. <P>2. Why did you like them?<BR>becuse it was so damn differnt<P>3. When and where did you first obtain your first Fiero?<BR>October 2000, Dallas TX<P>4. What type of Fiero do you own?<BR>'87 gt Fastback automatic<P>5. What year and model do you like the best?<BR>any gt fastback model<P>6. Do you have a nice paint job on it?<BR>looks like crap<P>7. What does it run like?<BR>cracked forward manifold sound like crap<P>8. Do you get "looks" when driving your Fiero?<BR>I dont drive it much, but the kid on my block all think it cool<P>9. What sound system do you have in your Fiero?<BR>The sounds of silence system. The stereo was stolen before I bought the car. and of course stereo is the last piece of the puzzle to pe put in.<P>10. Do your relatives and friends like Fieros?<BR>Most are stupid, they think they catch on fire for no reason. the think it is a very unsafe car.<P>11. Your Fiero?<BR>yes<P>12. Why do you think they cancelled the car (short answer please)?GM execs with boards up there @#%!<P>13. Do you want a new Fiero to be released?<BR>NO.<P>14. If so, what would you want it to look like?<P>15. What plans do you have for your Fiero, in terms of upgrades, engine work, body kits, sound system, etc..<P>RCC suspension and corvette brakes,northsar swap, 17"rims, artero nose, IRM rockers/scoops, hood vents, deck scoop(heat vent), pisa gt tail lights, 4.5 inch wing stantions  new euro style interior, kick ass stereo system, I would like to have archie chop the top, and last but not least painted some shade of orange<P>16. Do you think Fiero's will rise in collectors value?<BR> 88's will for sure also the rare ones.<P>17. If and when your Fiero finally does break down for good, will you keep it or junk it?<BR>If it ever does it will probably end up as an organ donor||||reg||1
Z||000063||Kevin-84SE||11-20-2000||01:08 PM||||1. When did you start to like Fieros? The first time I went for a ride in one in 1984<P>2. Why did you like them?  I liked the looks, I liked the handling, I liked the plastic body, Disc brakes, stainless exhaust. <P>3. When and where did you first obtain your first Fiero? I ordered one from a dealer in Poughkeepsie NY but I got tired of waiting and I found a dealer in Latham NY that had just gotten one in that had all the options that I wanted so I purchased it there in May of 1984.<P>4. What type of Fiero do you own? I still have my fully loaded Black 1984 Fiero SE<P>5. What year and model do you like the best? 1984 SE<P>6. Do you have a nice paint job on it? Yes, Factory Paint in excellent condition<P>7. What does it run like? I am currently trying to fix a stumble problem, other than that it runs very well, I took it on a 1500 mile trip to Michigan and back in August. <P>8. Do you get "looks" when driving your Fiero? Sometimes I do<P>9. What sound system do you have in your Fiero? Factory with Cassette and EQ plus a sub woofer behind the drivers seat<P>10. Do your relatives and friends like Fieros? Most do, my wife doesn't like fiero's much<P>11. Your Fiero? Oh yea, at least that's what they say<P>12. Why do you think they canceled the car (short answer please)? Bad reputation<P>13. Do you want a new Fiero to be released? I think a Fiero with today's technology would be great but I don't think will happen<P>14. If so, what would you want it to look like? I think the Fiero Styling is great so I would not want it to be much different <P>15. What plans do you have for your Fiero, in terms of upgrades, engine work, body kits, sound system, etc.. I would like to have my after-market rocker panels and rear spoiler repainted, they were painted without a clear-coat. I am considering digital gauges and I think I may pull the sub woofer out.  <P>16. Do you think Fiero's will rise in collectors value? Yes, I think they will eventually<P>17. If and when your Fiero finally does break down for good, will you keep it or junk it? If you mean that it is no longer derivable and is not repairable, I guess I would probably part it out.||||reg||7
Z||000064||PatrickB||11-20-2000||05:13 PM||||1. When did you start to like Fieros?<BR>I think around 2 years ago when my friend mentioned one and I was like what is that?   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/confused.gif"><P>2. Why did you like them?<BR> I checked them out and said hey I like this. After I took it out for I drive I said I want this! <P>3. When and where did you first obtain your first Fiero?<BR>From my friends friends roomates friend in Worcester MA.<P>4. What type of Fiero do you own?<BR> 86' Red GT<P>5. What year and model do you like the best?<BR> I would say 87' GT <P>6. Do you have a nice paint job on it?<BR>Awesome and original. <P> 7. What does it run like?<BR>Its getting there.  I think it sat for a while so some stuff went bad.  And some more old car maintainance.  <P> 8. Do you get "looks" when driving your Fiero?<BR>Not as many as I though. <P> 9. What sound system do you have in your Fiero?<BR>Ummmmm, not too much yet.  I got a nice new head unit and some kappa 4X10's that I got for free.<P>10. Do your relatives and friends like Fieros?<BR>Lets see,  wow thats small, hey dont they catch on fire, why is it so loud(new exhaust).... <P>11. Your Fiero?<BR>Up Above.  PS. They have grown to love it. <P>12. Why do you think they cancelled the car (short answer please)?<BR>The devil made them. <P>13. Do you want a new Fiero to be released?<BR>That would be cool.  I wouldnt be able to afford it but it would be cool to see as long as they dont kill it's heritage. <P>  14. If so, what would you want it to look like?<BR>I would say a 2 seater, tad bigger, bigger engine!, more of a newer style interior. <P> 15. What plans do you have for your Fiero, in terms of upgrades, engine work, body  kits, sound system, etc..<BR>Oh boy, I think you wanted a short answer so I will leave this blank. <P> 16. Do you think Fiero's will rise in collectors value?<BR>Honestly, not really.  I dont think they are in high enough demand except for us die hards. <P>17. If and when your Fiero finally does break down for good, will you keep it or junk it?<BR>Dont tell my car this but I would probably end up parting it out because I am a poor college student and wouldn't be able to afford to revive it. <p>[This message has been edited by PatrickB (edited 11-20-2000).]||||reg||14
Z||000065||MikeE||11-20-2000||06:42 PM||||I doubt if anyone will read this, but what the ****.<P>1. When did you start to like Fieros?<BR>From their inception in 1983.<P>2. Why did you like them?<BR>I liked the concept-affordable, stylish, mid-engine sports car.  Later I appreciated that they don't rust out in the harsh Hawaiian salt air and that, with a 5 star p & d crash rating, they are one of the safest small cars.<P>3. When and where did you first obtain your first Fiero?<BR>In 1993 I answered an ad for a non-running 86 2m4.  It was a parts car for the impound officer at the Kaneohe Marine base.  All he wanted was the O2 sensor but he removed the entire exhaust.  It was to be a project car but became a parts car after a 50' palm tree fell on it.<P>4. What type of Fiero do you own?<BR>86 2m4/5sp (parts car)<BR>87 2m4/5sp (needs mech work-future project)<BR>87 2m6/5sp (driving this one)<BR>all are black<P>5. What year and model do you like the best?I like all, but my favorites are:<BR>88 formula (w/spoiler removed)<BR>88 coupe (for mods/project)<P>6. Do you have a nice paint job on it?<BR>No-clear coat peeling from harsh Hawaiian sun.<P>7. What does it run like?<BR>Well for 99K mi but has the common erratic idle.<P>8. Do you get "looks" when driving your Fiero?<BR>No, unless you count disparaging glares over the loud (but stock) exhaust.<P>9. What sound system do you have in your Fiero?<BR>Stock w/bad right front speaker.<P>10. Do your relatives and friends like Fieros?<BR>I don't know.  My relatives are on the mainland and I don't talk to my wife's relatives due to language/culture issues.<P>11. Your Fiero?<BR>My wife hates it but tolerates it as long as I don't talk about it and it doesn't cost her any money (ignorance is bliss).<P>12. Why do you think they cancelled the car (short answer please)?<BR>I think it was just economics.  The costly 88 upgrades didn't raise sales so GM simply cut their losses.  I don't think it was ever a threat to the Corvette (except in someone's fantasy) but the early bad rep could have hurt sales.  For most people it just wasn't a practical car and it was hard/expensive to work on.<P>13. Do you want a new Fiero to be released?  Yes, if they kept to the original concept (affordable, stylish, mid-engine sports car) while modernizing it as with the Camaro/Firebird/Corvette.  The 2.4 twin cam four would be an affordable base engine and GM has many nice optional V6s, such as the 3.4 and the new 3.5 baby northstar.<P>14. If so, what would you want it to look like?<BR>A modern interpretation, as with the Camaro/Firebird/Corvette, or the retro cars from other manufacturers.<P>15. What plans do you have for your Fiero, in terms of upgrades, engine work, body kits, sound system, etc..<BR>All mods based on cost vs. effectivness on a budget, to be done on an 88.  First, general upgrades like better brakepads, stainless steel lines, etc.  Then taller (16"-18") wheels with low profile tires from some FWD special edition to keep costs down but still look unique, that will fill up wheel wells without having to lower the car (I already scrape things and can't get a jack under it).  Then I will engineer/install a 91 4.9L Cadillac aluminum V8 which will later be supercharged (just to be different).  Eventually I will paint it with the black cherry color used on late 80s corvettes (it looked black in indirect light).<P>16. Do you think Fiero's will rise in collectors value?<BR>Perhaps in time but not much.  Collector value requires both rarity and desirability.  Fieros aren't that rare and are only desirable to a few lunatic fringe like ourselves (and we always want a good deal).  Based on that, the 88s stand the best chance. <P>17. If and when your Fiero finally does break down for good, will you keep it or junk it?<BR>Mine are already gone to make way for an 88 project car (I'm still looking).  Since it will be a working canvas, I will most likely keep it until it is totalled, or I die.<P><P>------------------<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000066||MrPBody||11-20-2000||10:55 PM||||1. When did you start to like Fieros?<BR><B>1984</B><P>2. Why did you like them?<BR><B>Small, light, mid-engine</B><P>3. When and where did you first obtain your first Fiero?<BR><B>April, 2000</B><P>4. What type of Fiero do you own?<BR><B>1985 SE 4-cylinder 5-speed</B><P>5. What year and model do you like the best?<BR><B>1988 Formula</B><P>6. Do you have a nice paint job on it?<BR><B>Ask me next week.  (It's being painted.)</B><P>7. What does it run like?<BR><B>Like a stock 4-cylinder</B><P>8. Do you get "looks" when driving your Fiero?<BR><B>Depends on how crazily I'm driving</B><P>9. What sound system do you have in your Fiero?<BR><B>Stock</B><P>10. Do your relatives and friends like Fieros?<BR><B>Mixed; many skeptics</B><P>11. Your Fiero?<BR><B>Generally, yes</B><P>12. Why do you think they cancelled the car (short answer please)?<BR><B>Corporate paranoia; lack of imagination; committee-thinking; fiscal timidity; possible Corvette envy.  Pick as many as you like.</B><P>13. Do you want a new Fiero to be released?<BR><B>Pigs will fly first!  But yes.</B><P>14. If so, what would you want it to look like?<BR><B>I will get flamed for this -- late-model RX-7, Acura NSX, Toyota 2000 GT, Ferrari 512, or old Lola</B><P>15. What plans do you have for your Fiero, in terms of upgrades, engine work, body kits, sound system, etc..<BR><B>'87-88 coupe fascias, better anti-roll bars, suspension bushings, possible head porting.  A Quad4 swap sounds fun but too much work.</B><P>16. Do you think Fiero's will rise in collectors value?<BR><B>Maybe; probably not high.  But if people collect Edsels, anything's possible.</B><P>17. If and when your Fiero finally does break down for good, will you keep it or junk it?<BR><B>Keep it for parts and buy another one.</B><BR>||||reg||1
Z||000067||Jaygee79||11-20-2000||11:17 PM||||1. When did you start to like Fieros?<P>When I got mine.  I had never heard of them before that.<P>2. Why did you like them?<P>It was different.  A lot of cars look pretty much the same.  The look of the Fiero is unique.<P>3. When and where did you first obtain your first Fiero?<P>When I was 16.  A local TV show was giving away a car, all you had to do was write an essay on why you thought you should win it.  My mother wrote in and won.  She had a choice between the Fiero and a junky old Ford Fairmont.  She chose well   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>4. What type of Fiero do you own?<P>84 SE<P>5. What year and model do you like the best?<P>88 GT, of course<P>6. Do you have a nice paint job on it?<P>LOL that's funny.  If you saw my car you would know the answer to that question.Right now it looks sort of like someone dumped a bucket of brake fluid on it.<P>7. What does it run like?<P>Sometimes really good, sometimes like it's about to blow.  It depends on the mood of the car.<P>8. Do you get "looks" when driving your Fiero?<P>Sometimes<P>9. What sound system do you have in your Fiero?<P>Some radio that I got at Wal-Mart.  I want a nicer one, but I can't afford it yet.<P>10. Do your relatives and friends like Fieros?<P>Yes, I guess it's contagious   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>11.  Your Fiero?<P>I think so<P>12. Why do you think they cancelled the car (short answer please)?<P>Because it got a bad rep for fires and GM didn't make enough money on them.<P>13. Do you want a new Fiero to be released?<P>Yes and no.  I don't think that it would take away from the old Fiero's, they will always be the original Fiero's.<P>14. If so, what would you want it to look like?<P>Like the Fiero looks now, but a bit more updated.<P>15. What plans do you have for your Fiero, in terms of upgrades, engine work, body kits, sound system, etc..<P>New purple paint job (it'll look great, I swear), a V6 upgrade with an obvious rewiring job, power windows, mirrors and locks....pretty much everything new.<P>16. Do you think Fiero's will rise in collectors value?<P>Yes.  They have practically doubled since I have had mine.<P>17. If and when your Fiero finally does break down for good, will you keep it or junk it?<P>I'll keep it and make it look really great.  Then I'll tow it to shows and everyone will think that it's too nice to drive LOL<P><p>[This message has been edited by Jaygee79 (edited 11-20-2000).]||||reg||7
Z||000068||jerpro||11-21-2000||08:44 AM||||1. When did you start to like Fieros? 1999<BR>2. Why did you like them? Just came from barcelona, spain and fell in love at first sight.<P>3. When and where did you first obtain your first Fiero? Got it from a GM worker. I saw the car for sale all summer and bought it in sept. Bought my 87se shortly after that when I won a bet, but that is another story (hehehe)<P>4. What type of Fiero do you own?<BR>84se and 87se<BR>5. What year and model do you like the best?<BR>BOth. 84se is the beggining the classic, and the 87se is the beast.<BR>6. Do you have a nice paint job on it?<BR>Radar deflective paint on the 87se (hehehe)<P>7. What does it run like? <BR>84se still working on it.<BR>87se.. Corvette: "what the F#$% was that? <BR>GIrlfrien in the corvette: That was a fiero my dear.<BR>( a liiitle exagerated but good enough)<BR>8. Do you get "looks" when driving your Fiero? Strobe light inside the hood of the 87. pretty fun in the parking lots. <BR>HUge stereo system on the 84.<P>9. What sound system do you have in your Fiero?<BR>AN On the 84se <A HREF="http://www.perigee.net/~lunapark/pages/subw.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.perigee.net/~lunapark/pages/subw.html</A>  <BR>On the 87 se subwoof in the passenger side floor.<P>10. Do your relatives and friends like Fieros?<BR>except mom, all of them.<BR>11. Your Fiero?<BR>Girlfriend loves it. Especially the sunroof (hehehe)<BR>Father wants it.<BR>Brother desires it.<BR>Other brother drools on it.<BR>Friend hates me for it.<BR>Cousin gets orgasms from looking at it.<BR>NO one touches it.<BR>12. Why do you think they cancelled the car (short answer please)?<BR>Becuase they suck.<P>13. Do you want a new Fiero to be released?<P>YES&gt;<BR>14. If so, what would you want it to look like?<P>New concept car. Keep it in the same format but make it a liittle cubist ( like the Cadillac evoq )<BR>15. What plans do you have for your Fiero, in terms of upgrades, engine work, body kits, sound system, etc..<BR>1st. fix 84se and then put an adjustable timimng control.<BR>2nd. put some nitrous on 87se.<BR>16. Do you think Fiero's will rise in collectors value?<BR>No idea. They have never been too big. except the indy  ... AGHHHHHH (droool)<P>17. If and when your Fiero finally does break down for good, will you keep it or junk it?<BR>Fix it.<BR><P>------------------<BR>Only try your best, and if you don't succeed... TRY HARDER.||||reg||1
Z||000069||FieroLisa||11-21-2000||09:17 AM||||<BR>1. When did you start to like Fieros?<BR>When I was looking through the local auto trader. The first one I saw/looked at, I bought.<P>2. Why did you like them?<BR>Fairly inexpensive to work on, fun!!! basically i can afford it.<P>3. When and where did you first obtain your first Fiero?<BR>Canal Fulton OH, from some guy going to college (I was 15 at the time) um 3 years ago.<P>4. What type of Fiero do you own?<BR>86 all options gold 4 speed GT<BR>86 no options gold 5 speed SC<P>5. What year and model do you like the best?<BR>86 GT<P>6. Do you have a nice paint job on it?<BR>The coupe, yes- repainted light metallic gold. GT is still factory. Great paint to come.<P>7. What does it run like?<BR>GT is perfect, coupe is still very strong for 104K miles!<P>8. Do you get "looks" when driving your Fiero?<BR>Yep! That's why I drive it!<P>9. What sound system do you have in your Fiero?<BR>new bright blue display 40Wx4 Panasonic head unit, 300 watt amp, 10 inch crystal sub behind driver seat. Yes, its Loud.<BR>GT has the nice factory tape deck with equalizer, everything works, and its for sale (100 bucks)<P>10. Do your relatives and friends like Fieros?<BR>Ha! My dad hates em, my Mom was sick of mine taking up garage space, well thats why I always dated Fiero guys I guess!<P>11.  Your Fiero?<BR>Same thing- my friend called it a POS but thats only because I made her naseaus the way I drove it!<P>12. Why do you think they cancelled the car (short answer please)?<BR>WHatever it was, I'm pretty pissed. I rather liked the 89.<P>13. Do you want a new Fiero to be released?<BR>Maybe. I don't know. It's sort of nice having  discontinued car.<P>14. If so, what would you want it to look like?Like the 89! I think its a beautiful car, hardly outdated even now.<P>15. What plans do you have for your Fiero, in terms of upgrades, engine work, body kits, sound system, etc..<BR>coupe is all done and for sale. GT gets lowered 1.5", paint, 5Zigen Inperio 17in rims, redoing the interior in leather...blah blah blah...<P>16. Do you think Fiero's will rise in collectors value?honestly, not really.  Well maybe in many years if there are still low mileage ones, but those will be the only ones of value.<P>17. If and when your Fiero finally does break down for good, will you keep it or junk it?<BR>Probably part and sell. I;d need money for a new fiero!!!<BR><P>------------------<BR>Lisa<BR>86 gold 4 speed GT<BR>86 gold 5 speed SC (For Sale)<BR>Columbus, OH/Greensboro NC<BR>http://www.geocities.com/fierolisa/||||reg||12
Z||000070||Tigger||11-21-2000||09:25 AM||||1. When did you start to like Fieros?<BR>A: Before I could legally drive<P>2. Why did you like them?<BR>A: Dunno know, they're just cool!<P>3. When and where did you first obtain your first Fiero?<BR>A: June '99 <P>4. What type of Fiero do you own?<BR>A: '84 SE, 4 speed.<P>5. What year and model do you like the best?<BR>A: I like all years<P>6. Do you have a nice paint job on it?<BR>A: Yep, '69 Hugger Orange<P>7. What does it run like?<BR>A: Runs Great<P>8. Do you get "looks" when driving your Fiero?<BR>A: All the time<P>9. What sound system do you have in your Fiero?<BR>A: Original for now, priorities are elsewhere<P>10. Do your relatives and friends like Fieros?<BR>A: Yep, Father & Uncle are into them.<P>11.  Your Fiero?<BR>A: Yep<P>12. Why do you think they cancelled the car (short answer please)?<BR>A: Politics, started competing with the Vette.<P>13. Do you want a new Fiero to be released?<BR>A: Yes, but it would have to be a worthy design<P>14. If so, what would you want it to look like?<BR>A:  Overall similar design, tad bigger, some styling changes.<P>15. What plans do you have for your Fiero, in terms of upgrades, engine work, body kits, sound system, etc..<BR>A: Suspension upgrades, lower 2"<P>16. Do you think Fiero's will rise in collectors value?<BR>A: Yes<P>17. If and when your Fiero finally does break down for good, will you keep it or junk it?<BR>A: Going to keep it running as long as I possibly can<p>[This message has been edited by Tigger (edited 11-21-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000071||stsmithgt||11-21-2000||10:54 AM||||1.  It sounds bad, I was hitch hiking home on the freeway from a long night of partying and got picked up by a white fastback GT.(hmmmm just like the one I own now) I wonder if it's the same one?<P>2. I like the cockpit look nice style.<P>3. 1996 in Gilroy CA. bought it off a guy who was a broker for the original owner. Paid 2100.00 w\73,000 miles on it. everything works.<BR>a/c,cc/pl/pw/rear defrost/etc.<P>4.1986 GT white\grey interior 4spd.<P>5." " " " " " " " " " "<P>6.The paint need a little help due to key scratches and some cracking paint on the nose.  The bra takes care of that though. <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>7. For haveing 120,000 miles on it, it runs great.  Doesn't burn oil, but it does burn rubber.<P>8. I get more than the average looks due to being so handsome sitting in that beutiful car.(too much?) <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>9. My sound system is stock except for replacing the sub with a cheapo and the 4x10 by Pioneers.<P>10.  My sister in-law doesn't like it, but that "relative" everyone else thinks its nice and it fits my style.(cool)<P>11. Of course it's my Fiero.  With all the money I've put into it, right now it my hobbie.<P>12.  It doesn't fit the broad democratic sense of versatility.  They sold well, but they figured to sell more vetts and camaros with out having to deal with the fiero.  Nothing like feeling not needed after doing so well.<P>13.  If they released a new Fiero, it wouldn't be the same anyway.  Just leave them alone.<P>14.^^^^^^^^<P>15.side scoops, back deck scoop, front deck scoop.  I'm a scoopaholic. <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> 3.4 ugrade, better stereo, nicer paint. etc......<P>16.Eventually everything rises to collector state.  Look at the studabaker. Yuk.<P>17. It's a money pit.  Money pits can't be junked.  Fix it fix it fix it fix it......make it better.  Beware of the rust demon.||||reg||6
